{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LEtAv55nTQZa2h3M5mw8KW","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a complete picture. Let me create a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Complete Exploration of Drupal Migrate Suite Module\n\n### Directory Structure\n```\n/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/\n├── .chief/                           (Project management config)\n├── .claude/                          (Claude Code settings)\n├── .git/                             (Git repository)\n├── src/\n│   ├── Service/\n│   │   ├── MigrateMapQuery.php\n│   │   └── MigrateMessageQuery.php\n│   └── EventSubscriber/\n│       └── MigrateRunLogger.php\n├── migrate_suite.info.yml\n├── migrate_suite.services.yml\n├── migrate_suite.module\n├── migrate_suite.install\n├── PLAN.md\n└── progress.md\n```\n\n### No Submodules\nThere is **no modules/ directory** - this is a single parent module without submodules.\n\n---\n\n### Module Configuration Files\n\n#### 1. **migrate_suite.info.yml**\n- **Module Name:** Migrate Suite\n- **Type:** module\n- **Description:** Administration dashboard for managing and monitoring Drupal migrations.\n- **Package:** Migration\n- **Drupal Core Requirement:** ^10.4 || ^11\n- **Dependencies:** drupal:migrate (required)\n\n#### 2. **migrate_suite.services.yml**\nDefines three services:\n1. **migrate_suite.map_query** (MigrateMapQuery)\n   - Depends on: database, migration plugin manager\n   \n2. **migrate_suite.message_query** (MigrateMessageQuery)\n   - Depends on: database\n   \n3. **migrate_suite.run_logger** (MigrateRunLogger)\n   - Depends on: database, datetime.time\n   - Tagged as: event_subscriber\n\n#### 3. **migrate_suite.module**\nCurrently contains only the standard file header and documentation. No active hook implementations.\n\n#### 4. **migrate_suite.install**\nImplements `hook_schema()` with a single table:\n- **migrate_suite_run_log** - Stores migration run history with the following fields:\n  - `id` (serial, primary key)\n  - `migration_id` (varchar 255)\n  - `status` (varchar 32: idle, running, completed, failed)\n  - `started` (int timestamp)\n  - `finished` (int timestamp, nullable)\n  - `items_processed` (int, unsigned)\n  - `items_created` (int, unsigned)\n  - `items_updated` (int, unsigned)\n  - `items_failed` (int, unsigned)\n  - Indexes on migration_id and status\n\n---\n\n### PHP Classes\n\n#### 1. **MigrateMapQuery** (`/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/src/Service/MigrateMapQuery.php`)\nService for querying migration map tables. Methods:\n- `getMapTableName(string $migrationId): string` - Returns map table name (protected)\n- `lookupDestinationIds(string $migrationId, array $sourceIdValues): array` - Looks up destination IDs by source ID\n- `listImportedItems(string $migrationId, int $limit = 50, int $offset = 0): array` - Lists all imported items with pagination\n- `countItemsByStatus(string $migrationId): array` - Counts items by status (imported, needs_update, failed)\n\nUses Drupal's database API and migration plugin manager. Handles non-existent tables gracefully.\n\n#### 2. **MigrateMessageQuery** (`/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/src/Service/MigrateMessageQuery.php`)\nService for querying migration message tables. Methods:\n- `getMessageTableName(string $migrationId): string` - Returns message table name (protected)\n- `getMessages(string $migrationId, int $limit = 50, int $offset = 0): array` - Fetches messages with pagination\n- `getMessagesForSourceId(string $migrationId, array $sourceIdValues): array` - Fetches messages for a specific source ID\n\nUses Drupal's database API. Handles non-existent tables gracefully.\n\n#### 3. **MigrateRunLogger** (`/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/src/EventSubscriber/MigrateRunLogger.php`)\nEvent subscriber that logs migration run data. Implements `EventSubscriberInterface`.\n\n**Properties:**\n- `$activeRuns` - Tracks current run log IDs by migration ID\n- `$counters` - Tracks row-level counters (processed, created, updated, failed)\n\n**Subscribed Events:**\n- `PRE_IMPORT` → `onPreImport()`\n- `POST_IMPORT` → `onPostImport()`\n- `PRE_ROW_SAVE` → `onPreRowSave()`\n- `POST_ROW_SAVE` → `onPostRowSave()`\n\n**Logic:**\n- On pre-import: Creates a new run log entry with 'running' status\n- On pre-row-save: Increments processed counter\n- On post-row-save: Tracks created/updated/failed status based on row's destination IDs and status\n- On post-import: Updates run log with final counters and status (completed or failed based on presence of failures)\n\n---\n\n### Summary\nThis is a **parent migration suite module** that provides:\n- **Database logging** of migration runs with detailed statistics\n- **Query services** to retrieve migration map and message data\n- **Event subscription** to automatically track migration progress and outcomes\n- Support for **Drupal 10.4+ and 11**\n\nNo UI components or submodules are currently implemented - this is a backend infrastructure module."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a3518b3e5bace62ad (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 31378\ntool_uses: 12\nduration_ms: 22165</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"83d2f696-dcc4-44a7-bdc8-ff6d1a66e4a4","uuid":"81c1f7ae-c395-436e-955d-fc510713e08c","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the Drupal module at /Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite. I need to understand:\n1. All existing files and directory structure\n2. The contents of migrate_suite.info.yml, migrate_suite.services.yml, migrate_suite.module, migrate_suite.install\n3. The contents of all PHP files in src/\n4. Any existing submodule directories (modules/)\n\nBe thorough - read all files.","agentId":"a3518b3e5bace62ad","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a complete picture. Let me create a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Complete Exploration of Drupal Migrate Suite Module\n\n### Direc