{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V9wiPszVjkuq6KXvBMnJnJ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→## Codebase Patterns\n     2→- Module follows Drupal 10.4+/11.x coding standards with `declare(strict_types=1)` in PHP classes\n     3→- Services use constructor property promotion (`protected readonly`)\n     4→- Map tables follow Drupal migrate convention: `migrate_map_{migration_id}`\n     5→- Message tables follow: `migrate_message_{migration_id}`\n     6→- Source ID columns in map/message tables are `sourceid1`, `sourceid2`, etc. and `src_1`, `src_2` respectively\n     7→- Always inject services via constructor rather than using `\\Drupal::` static calls\n     8→- Services registered in `migrate_suite.services.yml`\n     9→- Submodules live in `modules/` directory (e.g., `modules/migrate_admin/`)\n    10→- Controllers use `ControllerBase` with `create()` for DI, not services.yml\n    11→- Migration group is accessed via `$migration->getPluginDefinition()['migration_group']`\n    12→- Use Drupal render arrays (`#type => 'table'`, `#type => 'details'`) for admin UI, not Twig templates\n    13→- Status badges use custom CSS classes (`color--success`, `color--error`, etc.)\n    14→\n    15→---\n    16→\n    17→## 2026-03-10 - US-001\n    18→- Implemented shared services in migrate_suite parent module\n    19→- Files created:\n    20→  - `migrate_suite.info.yml` - Module declaration with core migrate dependency\n    21→  - `migrate_suite.install` - Schema for `migrate_suite_run_log` table\n    22→  - `migrate_suite.module` - Module file\n    23→  - `migrate_suite.services.yml` - Service definitions\n    24→  - `src/Service/MigrateMapQuery.php` - Query service for migration map tables\n    25→  - `src/Service/MigrateMessageQuery.php` - Query service for migration message tables\n    26→  - `src/EventSubscriber/MigrateRunLogger.php` - Event subscriber for PRE_IMPORT, POST_IMPORT, PRE_ROW_SAVE, POST_ROW_SAVE\n    27→- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n    28→  - No phpcs/phpstan available locally; used `php -l` for syntax validation\n    29→  - Drupal migrate map tables use `source_row_status` column with MigrateIdMapInterface constants\n    30→  - This is a greenfield project - no existing code patterns to follow initially\n    31→  - The PRD may add `inProgress` field automatically; handle that when editing\n    32→---\n    33→\n    34→## 2026-03-10 - US-002\n    35→- Implemented migration overview dashboard page as `migrate_admin` submodule\n    36→- Files created:\n    37→  - `modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.info.yml` - Submodule declaration\n    38→  - `modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.module` - Module file\n    39→  - `modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.permissions.yml` - Dashboard permission\n    40→  - `modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.routing.yml` - Dashboard + detail routes\n    41→  - `modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.links.menu.yml` - Admin menu link\n    42→  - `modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.libraries.yml` - CSS library\n    43→  - `modules/migrate_admin/css/migrate_admin.css` - Status badge and filter styling\n    44→  - `modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDashboardController.php` - Dashboard controller\n    45→- Features: migration listing with grouping, collapsible sections, status badges, filter form, empty state, detail page placeholder\n    46→- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n    47→  - Migration group is in plugin definition, not a direct method on MigrationInterface\n    48→  - Use `#type => 'details'` with `#open => TRUE` for collapsible grouped sections\n    49→  - Dashboard links to detail route `migrate_admin.migration_detail` with `{migration_id}` parameter\n    50→  - Filter form uses plain HTML form (GET method) since we don't need CSRF for read-only filters\n    51→  - PRD auto-adds `inProgress` field; remove it when setting `passes: true`\n    52→---\n    53→\n    54→## 2026-03-10 - US-003\n    55→- Implemented migration detail page with imported items table and messages tab\n    56→- Files created:\n    57→  - `modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDetailController.php` - New controller for detail and messages pages\n    58→- Files modified:\n    59→  - `modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.routing.yml` - Added messages route, updated detail route to new controller\n    60→  - `modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDashboardController.php` - Removed placeholder detail() method\n    61→  - `modules/migrate_admin/css/migrate_admin.css` - Added tab navigation and pager styles\n    62→- Features: summary section (label, group, source/dest plugins, status, last run stats), imported items table with source IDs, entity links, status, last import timestamp, 50-item pagination, source ID search filter, status dropdown filter, messages tab with severity icons and severity filter\n    63→- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n    64→  - Detail controller uses `loadMigration()` helper that throws NotFoundHttpException for invalid migration IDs\n    65→  - Entity linking works by parsing `entity:{type}` from destination plugin definition\n    66→  - Message severity uses RFC 5424 levels: 3=error, 4=warning, 5+=notice\n    67→  - Map table columns: `sourceid1..N`, `destid1..N`, `source_row_status`, `last_imported`\n    68→  - Message table columns: `src_1..N`, `level`, `message`\n    69→  - Use `clone $query` then `countQuery()` for total count before applying `range()` for pagination\n    70→  - Tabs are implemented as plain links with CSS styling, not Drupal's local tasks (since both pages share the same permission)\n    71→---\n    72→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ff06007-d15b-4e19-9bb5-ef9d85432d82","uuid":"914fa066-c3be-4d02-b46b-789dde8c9a64","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/progress.md","content":"## Codebase Patterns\n- Module follows Drupal 10.4+/11.x coding standards with `declare(strict_types=1)` in PHP classes\n- Services use constructor property promotion (`protected readonly`)\n- Map tables follow Drupal migrate convention: `migrate_map_{migration_id}`\n- Message tables follow: `migrate_message_{migration_id}`\n- Source ID columns in map/message tables are `sourceid1`, `sourceid2`, etc. and `src_1`, `src_2` respectively\n- Always inject services via constructor rather than using `\\Drupal::` static calls\n- Services registered in `migrate_suite.services.yml`\n- Submodules live in `modules/` directory (e.g., `modules/migrate_admin/`)\n- Controllers use `ControllerBase` with `create()` for DI, not services.yml\n- Migration group is accessed via `$migration->getPluginDefinition()['migration_group']`\n- Use Drupal render arrays (`#type => 'table'`, `#type => 'details'`) for admin UI, not Twig templates\n- Status badges use custom CSS classes (`color--success`, `color--error`, etc.)\n\n---\n\n## 2026-03-10 - US-001\n- Implemented shared services in migrate_suite parent module\n- Files created:\n  - `migrate_suite.info.yml` - Module declaration with core migrate dependency\n  - `migrate_suite.install` - Schema for `migrate_suite_run_log` table\n  - `migrate_suite.module` - Module file\n  - `migrate_suite.services.yml` - Service definitions\n  - `src/Service/MigrateMapQuery.php` - Query service for migration map tables\n  - `src/Service/MigrateMessageQuery.php` - Query service for migration message tables\n  - `src/EventSubscriber/MigrateRunLogger.php` - Event subscriber for PRE_IMPORT, POST_IMPORT, PRE_ROW_SAVE, POST_ROW_SAVE\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - No phpcs/phpstan available locally; used `php -l` for syntax validation\n  - Drupal migrate map tables use `source_row_status` column with MigrateIdMapInterface constants\n  - This is a greenfield project - no existing code patterns to follow initially\n  - The PRD may add `inProgress` field automatically; handle that when editing\n---\n\n## 2026-03-10 - US-002\n- Implemented migration overview dashboard page as `migrate_admin` submodule\n- Files created:\n  - `modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.info.yml` - Submodule declaration\n  - `modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.module` - Module file\n  - `modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.permissions.yml` - Dashboard permission\n  - `modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.routing.yml` - Dashboard + detail routes\n  - `modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.links.menu.yml` - Admin menu link\n  - `modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.libraries.yml` - CSS library\n  - `modules/migrate_admin/css/migrate_admin.css` - Status badge and filter styling\n  - `modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDashboardController.php` - Dashboard controller\n- Features: migration listing with grouping, collapsible sections, status badges, filter form, empty state, detail page placeholder\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - Migration group is in plugin definition, not a direct method on MigrationInterface\n  - Use `#type => 'details'` with `#open => TRUE` for collapsible grouped sections\n  - Dashboard links to detail route `migrate_admin.migration_detail` with `{migration_id}` parameter\n  - Filter form uses plain HTML form (GET method) since we don't need CSRF for read-only filters\n  - PRD auto-adds `inProgress` field; remove it when setting `passes: true`\n---\n\n## 2026-03-10 - US-003\n- Implemented migration detail page with imported items table and messages tab\n- Files created:\n  - `modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDetailController.php` - New controller for detail and messages pages\n- Files modified:\n  - `modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.routing.yml` - Added messages route, updated detail route to new controller\n  - `modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDashboardController.php` - Removed placeholder detail() method\n  - `modules/migrate_admin/css/migrate_admin.css` - Added tab navigation and pager styles\n- Features: summary section (label, group, source/dest plugins, status, last run stats), imported items table with source IDs, entity links, status, last import timestamp, 50-item pagination, source ID search filter, status dropdown filter, messages tab with severity icons and severity filter\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - Detail controller uses `loadMigration()` helper that throws NotFoundHttpException for invalid migration IDs\n  - Entity linking works by parsing `entity:{type}` from destination plugin definition\n  - Message severity uses RFC 5424 levels: 3=error, 4=warning, 5+=notice\n  - Map table columns: `sourceid1..N`, `destid1..N`, `source_row_status`, `last_imported`\n  - Message table columns: `src_1..N`, `level`, `message`\n  - Use `clone $query` then `countQuery()` for total count before applying `range()` for pagination\n  - Tabs are implemented as plain links with CSS styling, not Drupal's local tasks (since both pages share the same permission)\n---\n","numLines":72,"startLine":1,"totalLines":72}}}
