{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YQpbM5YUa7uWExQhuuSjjV","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary of the project structure:\n\n## Complete Drupal Migrate Suite Project Exploration\n\nI've thoroughly explored the Drupal migrate_suite project. Here's a comprehensive report:\n\n---\n\n## 1. COMPLETE FILE STRUCTURE\n\n```\n/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/\n├── migrate_suite.info.yml                          # Parent module definition\n├── migrate_suite.module                            # Parent module hooks\n├── migrate_suite.install                           # Install hooks and schema\n├── migrate_suite.services.yml                      # Parent module services\n├── PLAN.md                                         # Project plan documentation\n├── progress.md                                     # Progress tracking\n├── .chief/                                         # Chief configuration\n│   ├── config.yaml\n│   └── prds/main/\n│       ├── prd.md\n│       ├── prd.json\n│       └── claude.log\n├── .claude/\n│   └── settings.local.json\n├── modules/\n│   └── migrate_admin/                              # Admin dashboard submodule\n│       ├── migrate_admin.info.yml\n│       ├── migrate_admin.module\n│       ├── migrate_admin.routing.yml\n│       ├── migrate_admin.permissions.yml\n│       ├── migrate_admin.links.menu.yml\n│       ├── migrate_admin.libraries.yml\n│       ├── css/\n│       │   └── migrate_admin.css\n│       └── src/Controller/\n│           ├── MigrationDashboardController.php\n│           └── MigrationDetailController.php\n└── src/\n    ├── Service/\n    │   ├── MigrateMapQuery.php\n    │   └── MigrateMessageQuery.php\n    └── EventSubscriber/\n        └── MigrateRunLogger.php\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. migrate_admin.routing.yml\n\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.routing.yml`\n\nDefines 3 routes:\n- **migrate_admin.dashboard**: Main dashboard at `/admin/structure/migrate-suite`\n- **migrate_admin.migration_detail**: Detail page for individual migrations at `/admin/structure/migrate-suite/{migration_id}`\n- **migrate_admin.migration_messages**: Messages page at `/admin/structure/migrate-suite/{migration_id}/messages`\n\nAll routes require `view migrate suite dashboard` permission and are handled by MigrationDashboardController and MigrationDetailController.\n\n---\n\n## 3. migrate_admin.permissions.yml\n\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.permissions.yml`\n\nDefines a single permission:\n- **view migrate suite dashboard**: Title \"View Migrate Suite dashboard\" - grants access to view migration dashboard and check migration status\n\n---\n\n## 4. MigrationDashboardController.php\n\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDashboardController.php`\n\n**Key Features:**\n- **Dependencies:** MigrationPluginManager, Database, DateFormatter\n- **Main method:** `dashboard()` - Renders migration overview dashboard\n- **Key functionality:**\n  - Retrieves all migrations via plugin manager\n  - Supports filtering by: search text, status (idle/importing/rolling_back/completed/failed), and migration group\n  - Groups migrations by group name\n  - Displays for each migration:\n    - Label and group\n    - Status with colored badges\n    - Source item count\n    - Imported/failed item counts\n    - Last run timestamp\n  - Builds dynamic filter form with search, status, and group dropdowns\n  - Queries `migrate_map_*` tables for item counts\n  - Queries `migrate_suite_run_log` table for status and timestamps\n  - Links migration names to detail page\n  - Implements pagination via details/collapsible groups\n  - Cache contexts on query args and migration_plugins tag\n\n**Helper methods:**\n- `getMigrationStatus()`: Maps Drupal migration status to dashboard statuses\n- `getItemCounts()`: Counts imported/needs_update/failed items from map table\n- `getSourceCount()`: Gets source plugin item count\n- `getLastRunTimestamp()`: Queries run log\n- `buildFilterForm()`: Creates HTML form for filtering\n- `buildGroupTable()`: Renders collapsible group tables\n- `buildStatusBadge()`: Creates colored status badges\n\n---\n\n## 5. MigrationDetailController.php\n\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDetailController.php`\n\n**Key Features:**\n- **Dependencies:** MigrationPluginManager, Database, DateFormatter\n- **Main methods:**\n  - `detail()`: Detail page with imported items tab\n  - `messages()`: Messages tab showing migration warnings/errors\n  - `loadMigration()`: Loads migration or throws 404\n- **Pagination:** 50 items per page (ITEMS_PER_PAGE constant)\n\n**Detail Page Features:**\n- Summary section showing:\n  - Migration label and group\n  - Source/destination plugins\n  - Current status with badge\n  - Last run summary (started/finished dates, item counts)\n- Two tabs: \"Imported Items\" and \"Messages\"\n- Imported Items section:\n  - Filter by source ID (search) and status (imported/needs_update/failed)\n  - Table columns: Source ID(s), Destination entity, Status, Last import\n  - Attempts to link destination IDs to entities\n  - Pagination with Previous/Next buttons\n  - Queries `migrate_map_*` table\n  - Dynamically detects sourceid/destid columns (up to 9 each)\n  \n**Messages Page Features:**\n- Filter by severity (notice/warning/error)\n- Table columns: Source ID(s), Severity icon, Message\n- Pagination support\n- Queries `migrate_message_*` table\n- Maps RFC 5424 severity levels to user-friendly badges\n\n**Helper methods:**\n- `getMigrationStatus()`: Maps status strings\n- `getLastRunStats()`: Fetches run log data\n- `buildLastRunSummary()`: Formats last run information\n- `buildStatusBadge()`: Creates status badges\n- `buildImportedItemsSection()`: Renders items with filters/pager\n- `buildMessagesSection()`: Renders messages with filters/pager\n- `buildItemFilterForm()` / `buildMessageFilterForm()`: Filter UI\n- `buildPager()`: Creates pagination links\n- `getRowStatusLabel()`: Maps status codes to labels (0=imported, 1=needs_update, 2=failed)\n- `getSeverityIcon()`: Maps RFC 5424 levels to badge HTML\n- `buildEntityLink()`: Attempts to create links to destination entities\n- `buildSelectOptions()`: Renders HTML option elements\n\n---\n\n## 6. migrate_suite.services.yml\n\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/migrate_suite.services.yml`\n\nDefines 3 services:\n\n1. **migrate_suite.map_query**\n   - Class: `Drupal\\migrate_suite\\Service\\MigrateMapQuery`\n   - Dependencies: `@database`, `@plugin.manager.migration`\n   - Purpose: Query migration map tables\n\n2. **migrate_suite.message_query**\n   - Class: `Drupal\\migrate_suite\\Service\\MigrateMessageQuery`\n   - Dependencies: `@database`\n   - Purpose: Query migration message tables\n\n3. **migrate_suite.run_logger**\n   - Class: `Drupal\\migrate_suite\\EventSubscriber\\MigrateRunLogger`\n   - Dependencies: `@database`, `@datetime.time`\n   - Tags: `event_subscriber`\n   - Purpose: Listen to migration events and log run data\n\n---\n\n## ADDITIONAL KEY COMPONENTS\n\n### MigrateMapQuery Service\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/src/Service/MigrateMapQuery.php`\n\n**Methods:**\n- `lookupDestinationIds()`: Find destination IDs by source ID values\n- `listImportedItems()`: Paginated list of imported items\n- `countItemsByStatus()`: Count items by status (imported/needs_update/failed)\n\nUses `migrate_map_*` tables. Maps status constants: 0=imported, 1=needs_update, 2=failed\n\n### MigrateMessageQuery Service\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/src/Service/MigrateMessageQuery.php`\n\n**Methods:**\n- `getMessages()`: Fetch paginated messages for a migration\n- `getMessagesForSourceId()`: Fetch messages for specific source ID(s)\n\nUses `migrate_message_*` tables with columns: `src_1` through `src_9` for source IDs\n\n### MigrateRunLogger Event Subscriber\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/src/EventSubscriber/MigrateRunLogger.php`\n\n**Events subscribed:**\n- `PRE_IMPORT`: Creates run log entry with status=running\n- `POST_IMPORT`: Updates run log with final status (completed/failed) and counters\n- `PRE_ROW_SAVE`: Increments processed counter\n- `POST_ROW_SAVE`: Tracks created/updated/failed counters based on source_row_status\n\n**Custom Database Table:**\n- `migrate_suite_run_log`: Stores migration run history with status, timestamps, and item counts\n\n### migrate_suite.install\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/migrate_suite.install`\n\nDefines schema for `migrate_suite_run_log` table:\n- **Columns:**\n  - id (serial primary key)\n  - migration_id (varchar, indexed)\n  - status (varchar: idle/running/completed/failed, indexed)\n  - started (int timestamp)\n  - finished (int timestamp, nullable)\n  - items_processed, items_created, items_updated, items_failed (unsigned ints)\n\n---\n\n## MODULE DEPENDENCIES & METADATA\n\n**migrate_suite.info.yml:**\n- Name: Migrate Suite\n- Type: module\n- Core requirement: ^10.4 || ^11\n- Dependencies: drupal:migrate\n\n**migrate_admin.info.yml:**\n- Name: Migrate Admin\n- Type: module\n- Core requirement: ^10.4 || ^11\n- Dependencies: migrate_suite:migrate_suite\n\n**Menu link:**\n- Route: migrate_admin.dashboard\n- Parent: system.admin_structure\n- Title: Migration Dashboard\n- Weight: 50\n\n**Styling:**\n- Library: migrate_admin/dashboard\n- CSS file: migrate_admin.css\n- Defines badge styling and form/tab/pager styling\n\n---\n\n## ARCHITECTURE SUMMARY\n\nThe project follows a clean separation of concerns:\n\n1. **Parent module (migrate_suite):** Provides core services and database infrastructure\n2. **Admin submodule (migrate_admin):** Provides web UI for monitoring migrations\n3. **Services:** Reusable query classes for map and message tables\n4. **Event subscriber:** Automatically logs migration execution details\n5. **Controllers:** Generate dynamic UI based on migration data\n6. **Database:** Custom table tracks run history; utilizes Drupal's native migrate_map_* and migrate_message_* tables"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a387814587c7ba4ee (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 54999\ntool_uses: 16\nduration_ms: 46119</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ff06007-d15b-4e19-9bb5-ef9d85432d82","uuid":"43b608a1-6d5e-4f71-9de4-7348ce473c61","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the Drupal migrate_suite project at /Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite. I need to understand:\n1. The full file structure (all files)\n2. The contents of modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.routing.yml\n3. The contents of modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.permissions.yml\n4. The MigrationDashboardController.php \n5. The MigrationDetailController.php\n6. The migrate_suite.services.yml\n\nBe thorough - read all these files completely.","agentId":"a387814587c7ba4ee","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary of the project structure:\n\n## Complete Drupal Migrate Suite Project Exploration\n\nI've thoroughly explored the Drupal migrate_suite project. Here's a comprehensive report:\n\n---\n\n## 1. COMPLETE FILE STRUCTURE\n\n```\n/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/\n├── migrate_suite.info.yml                          # Parent module definition\n├── migrate_suite.module                            # Parent module hooks\n├── migrate_suite.install                           # Install hooks and schema\n├── migrate_suite.services.yml                      # Parent module services\n├── PLAN.md                                         # Project plan documentation\n├── progress.md                                     # Progress tracking\n├── .chief/                                         # Chief configuration\n│   ├── config.yaml\n│   └── prds/main/\n│       ├── prd.md\n│       ├── prd.json\n│       └── claude.log\n├── .claude/\n│   └── settings.local.json\n├── modules/\n│   └── migrate_admin/                              # Admin dashboard submodule\n│       ├── migrate_admin.info.yml\n│       ├── migrate_admin.module\n│       ├── migrate_admin.routing.yml\n│       ├── migrate_admin.permissions.yml\n│       ├── migrate_admin.links.menu.yml\n│       ├── migrate_admin.libraries.yml\n│       ├── css/\n│       │   └── migrate_admin.css\n│       └── src/Controller/\n│           ├── MigrationDashboardController.php\n│           └── MigrationDetailController.php\n└── src/\n    ├── Service/\n    │   ├── MigrateMapQuery.php\n    │   └── MigrateMessageQuery.php\n    └── EventSubscriber/\n        └── MigrateRunLogger.php\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. migrate_admin.routing.yml\n\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.routing.yml`\n\nDefines 3 routes:\n- **migrate_admin.dashboard**: Main dashboard at `/admin/structure/migrate-suite`\n- **migrate_admin.migration_detail**: Detail page for individual migrations at `/admin/structure/migrate-suite/{migration_id}`\n- **migrate_admin.migration_messages**: Messages page at `/admin/structure/migrate-suite/{migration_id}/messages`\n\nAll routes require `view migrate suite dashboard` permission and are handled by MigrationDashboardController and MigrationDetailController.\n\n---\n\n## 3. migrate_admin.permissions.yml\n\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.permissions.yml`\n\nDefines a single permission:\n- **view migrate suite dashboard**: Title \"View Migrate Suite dashboard\" - grants access to view migration dashboard and check migration status\n\n---\n\n## 4. MigrationDashboardController.php\n\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDashboardController.php`\n\n**Key Features:**\n- **Dependencies:** MigrationPluginManager, Database, DateFormatter\n- **Main method:** `dashboard()` - Renders migration overview dashboard\n- **Key functionality:**\n  - Retrieves all migrations via plugin manager\n  - Supports filtering by: search text, status (idle/importing/rolling_back/completed/failed), and migration group\n  - Groups migrations by group name\n  - Displays for each migration:\n    - Label and group\n    - Status with colored badges\n    - Source item count\n    - Imported/failed item counts\n    - Last run timestamp\n  - Builds dynamic filter form with search, status, and group dropdowns\n  - Queries `migrate_map_*` tables for item counts\n  - Queries `migrate_suite_run_log` table for status and timestamps\n  - Links migration names to detail page\n  - Implements pagination via details/collapsible groups\n  - Cache contexts on query args and migration_plugins tag\n\n**Helper methods:**\n- `getMigrationStatus()`: Maps Drupal migration status to dashboard statuses\n- `getItemCounts()`: Counts imported/needs_update/failed items from map table\n- `getSourceCount()`: Gets source plugin item count\n- `getLastRunTimestamp()`: Queries run log\n- `buildFilterForm()`: Creates HTML form for filtering\n- `buildGroupTable()`: Renders collapsible group tables\n- `buildStatusBadge()`: Creates colored status badges\n\n---\n\n## 5. MigrationDetailController.php\n\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDetailController.php`\n\n**Key Features:**\n- **Dependencies:** MigrationPluginManager, Database, DateFormatter\n- **Main methods:**\n  - `detail()`: Detail page with imported items tab\n  - `messages()`: Messages tab showing migration warnings/errors\n  - `loadMigration()`: Loads migration or throws 404\n- **Pagination:** 50 items per page (ITEMS_PER_PAGE constant)\n\n**Detail Page Features:**\n- Summary section showing:\n  - Migration label and group\n  - Source/destination plugins\n  - Current status with badge\n  - Last run summary (started/finished dates, item counts)\n- Two tabs: \"Imported Items\" and \"Messages\"\n- Imported Items section:\n  - Filter by source ID (search) and status (imported/needs_update/failed)\n  - Table columns: Source ID(s), Destination entity, Status, Last import\n  - Attempts to link destination IDs to entities\n  - Pagination with Previous/Next buttons\n  - Queries `migrate_map_*` table\n  - Dynamically detects sourceid/destid columns (up to 9 each)\n  \n**Messages Page Features:**\n- Filter by severity (notice/warning/error)\n- Table columns: Source ID(s), Severity icon, Message\n- Pagination support\n- Queries `migrate_message_*` table\n- Maps RFC 5424 severity levels to user-friendly badges\n\n**Helper methods:**\n- `getMigrationStatus()`: Maps status strings\n- `getLastRunStats()`: Fetches run log data\n- `buildLastRunSummary()`: Formats last run information\n- `buildStatusBadge()`: Creates status badges\n- `buildImportedItemsSection()`: Renders items with filters/pager\n- `buildMessagesSection()`: Renders messages with filters/pager\n- `buildItemFilterForm()` / `buildMessageFilterForm()`: Filter UI\n- `buildPager()`: Creates pagination links\n- `getRowStatusLabel()`: Maps status codes to labels (0=imported, 1=needs_update, 2=failed)\n- `getSeverityIcon()`: Maps RFC 5424 levels to badge HTML\n- `buildEntityLink()`: Attempts to create links to destination entities\n- `buildSelectOptions()`: Renders HTML option elements\n\n---\n\n## 6. migrate_suite.services.yml\n\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/migrate_suite.services.yml`\n\nDefines 3 services:\n\n1. **migrate_suite.map_query**\n   - Class: `Drupal\\migrate_suite\\Service\\MigrateMapQuery`\n   - Dependencies: `@database`, `@plugin.manager.migration`\n   - Purpose: Query migration map tables\n\n2. **migrate_suite.message_query**\n   - Class: `Drupal\\migrate_suite\\Service\\MigrateMessageQuery`\n   - Dependencies: `@database`\n   - Purpose: Query migration message tables\n\n3. **migrate_suite.run_logger**\n   - Class: `Drupal\\migrate_suite\\EventSubscriber\\MigrateRunLogger`\n   - Dependencies: `@database`, `@datetime.time`\n   - Tags: `event_subscriber`\n   - Purpose: Listen to migration events and log run data\n\n---\n\n## ADDITIONAL KEY COMPONENTS\n\n### MigrateMapQuery Service\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/src/Service/MigrateMapQuery.php`\n\n**Methods:**\n- `lookupDestinationIds()`: Find destination IDs by source ID values\n- `listImportedItems()`: Paginated list of imported items\n- `countItemsByStatus()`: Count items by status (imported/needs_update/failed)\n\nUses `migrate_map_*` tables. Maps status constants: 0=imported, 1=needs_update, 2=failed\n\n### MigrateMessageQuery Service\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/src/Service/MigrateMessageQuery.php`\n\n**Methods:**\n- `getMessages()`: Fetch paginated messages for a migration\n- `getMessagesForSourceId()`: Fetch messages for specific source ID(s)\n\nUses `migrate_message_*` tables with columns: `src_1` through `src_9` for source IDs\n\n### MigrateRunLogger Event Subscriber\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/src/EventSubscriber/MigrateRunLogger.php`\n\n**Events subscribed:**\n- `PRE_IMPORT`: Creates run log entry with status=running\n- `POST_IMPORT`: Updates run log with final status (completed/failed) and counters\n- `PRE_ROW_SAVE`: Increments processed counter\n- `POST_ROW_SAVE`: Tracks created/updated/failed counters based on source_row_status\n\n**Custom Database Table:**\n- `migrate_suite_run_log`: Stores migration run history with status, timestamps, and item counts\n\n### migrate_suite.install\n**Location:** `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/migrate_suite.install`\n\nDefines schema for `migrate_suite_run_log` table:\n- **Columns:**\n  - id (serial primary key)\n  - migration_id (varchar, indexed)\n  - status (varchar: idle/running/completed/failed, indexed)\n  - started (int timestamp)\n  - finished (int timestamp, nullable)\n  - items_processed, items_created, items_updated, items_failed (unsigned ints)\n\n---\n\n## MODULE DEPENDENCIES & METADATA\n\n**migrate_suite.info.yml:**\n- Name: Migrate Suite\n- Type: module\n- Core requirement: ^10.4 || ^11\n- Dependencies: drupal:migrate\n\n**migrate_admin.info.yml:**\n- Name: Migrate Admin\n- Type: module\n- Core requirement: ^10.4 || ^11\n- Dependencies: migrate_suite:migrate_suite\n\n**Menu link:**\n- Route: migrate_admin.dashboard\n- Parent: system.admin_structure\n- Title: Migration Dashboard\n- Weight: 50\n\n**Styling:**\n- Library: migrate_admin/dashboard\n- CSS file: migrate_admin.css\n- Defines badge styling and form/tab/pager styling\n\n---\n\n## ARCHITECTURE SUMMARY\n\nThe project follows a clean separation of concerns:\n\n1. **Parent module (migrate_suite):** Provides core services and database infrastructure\n2. **Admin submodule (migrate_admin):** Provides web UI for monitoring migrations\n3. **Services:** Reusable query classes for map and message tables\n4. **Event subscriber:** Automatically logs migration execution details\n5. **Controllers:** Generate dynamic UI based on migration data\n6. **Database:** Custom table tracks run history; utilizes Drupal's native migrate_map_* and migrate_message_* tables"}],"totalDurationMs":46119,"totalTokens":54999,"totalToolUseCount":16,"usage":{"input_tokens":838,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2829,"cache_read_input_tokens":48563,"output_tokens":2769,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2829},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CpmEH6tcnWQqakw3eJvgxA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good understanding of the codebase. Let me implement US-004: Per-migration view permissions.\n\nKey requirements:\n1. `migrate_permissions.info.yml` - new submodule\n2. Dynamic permission callback generating `view migration {migration_id}` for each migration\n3. Permissions appear in Drupal's standard permissions page under \"Migrate Suite\" group\n4. Dashboard (US-002) filters based on per-migration view permissions\n5. Detail page (US-003) checks per-migration view permission\n6. Empty dashboard with help message when user has dashboard permission but no per-migration permissions\n7. Users with `administer migrations` or `administer site configuration` bypass per-migration checks\n\n\n8. Permission names derived from migration plugin ID (machine-safe)\n\nI'll start by creating the module structure with the info file, then build out the dynamic permission callback that generates permissions for each migration, and finally integrate the access checks into the dashboard and detail controllers.\n\nFor the permission callbacks, I'm setting up a class that generates permissions like `view migration article_migration` for each registered migration plugin. The key challenge is handling the bypass logic—both `administer migrations` and `administer site configuration` should skip per-migration checks. I'm thinking a service approach would be cleanest for filtering migrations on the dashboard based on what the current user can access.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3135,"cache_read_input_tokens":35666,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3135},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ff06007-d15b-4e19-9bb5-ef9d85432d82","uuid":"f2dad3e8-9514-4486-a793-db84c93cbd41"}
