{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JAmBAdd5ZHjEG9NHm5kRWQ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary of all the files I've read:\n\n## Complete Codebase Exploration Report\n\nI have thoroughly explored the migrate_suite Drupal module codebase and read all requested files. Here's the complete breakdown:\n\n### 1. MIGRATE_PERMISSIONS SUBMODULE STRUCTURE\n\n**All files in `/modules/migrate_permissions/`:**\n\n#### migrate_permissions.info.yml\n```yaml\nname: Migrate Permissions\ntype: module\ndescription: 'Provides granular per-migration permissions integrated with Drupal''s permission system.'\npackage: Migrate Suite\ncore_version_requirement: ^10.4 || ^11\ndependencies:\n  - migrate_suite:migrate_suite\n```\n\n#### migrate_permissions.module\n```php\n<?php\n\n/**\n * @file\n * Provides per-migration permissions for Migrate Suite.\n */\n```\n\n#### migrate_permissions.permissions.yml\n```yaml\npermission_callbacks:\n  - Drupal\\migrate_permissions\\MigratePermissions::permissions\n```\n\n#### migrate_permissions.services.yml\n```yaml\nservices:\n  migrate_permissions.access_check:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_permissions\\MigrateAccessCheck\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. MIPIGRATE PERMISSIONS CLASS\n**File: `/modules/migrate_permissions/src/MigratePermissions.php`**\n\nComplete PHP class that implements `ContainerInjectionInterface` and provides dynamic per-migration permissions. Key features:\n- Iterates through all migrations to generate permission definitions\n- Creates permission names using sanitized migration IDs (lowercase, alphanumeric + underscores)\n- Format: `view migration {safe_id}`\n- Each permission has a title and description\n- Gracefully handles exceptions when loading migrations\n\n---\n\n### 3. MIGRATE ACCESS CHECK CLASS\n**File: `/modules/migrate_permissions/src/MigrateAccessCheck.php`**\n\nSimple permission checker with one key method `canViewMigration()`:\n- Bypasses checks for users with 'administer migrations' or 'administer site configuration' permissions\n- Checks for per-migration view permission using sanitized migration ID\n- Returns boolean indicating whether user can view a specific migration\n\n---\n\n### 4. MIGRATION DASHBOARD CONTROLLER\n**File: `/modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDashboardController.php`**\n\nComprehensive controller (546 lines) with these key methods:\n- `dashboard()`: Main page builder that:\n  - Accepts search, status, and group filters via query parameters\n  - Applies per-migration view permissions if migrate_permissions module is enabled\n  - Groups migrations by their migration_group\n  - Builds filter form and migration group tables\n  - Caches results with migration_plugins tag\n  \n- Helper methods:\n  - `getMigrationStatus()`: Maps Drupal status labels to internal statuses (idle, importing, rolling_back, completed, failed)\n  - `getItemCounts()`: Queries migrate_map table for imported/failed/needs_update counts\n  - `getSourceCount()`: Gets source plugin item count\n  - `getLastRunTimestamp()`: Retrieves last run timestamp from migrate_suite_run_log\n  - `buildFilterForm()`: Creates HTML filter form with search, status, and group dropdowns\n  - `buildGroupTable()`: Creates details element with migration table for each group\n  - `buildStatusBadge()`: Creates colored badge spans\n\n---\n\n### 5. MIGRATION DETAIL CONTROLLER\n**File: `/modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDetailController.php`**\n\nLarge controller (912 lines) handling two main pages with these key methods:\n- `detail()`: Imported items page with:\n  - Summary section showing migration metadata\n  - Tab navigation between \"Imported Items\" and \"Messages\"\n  - Imported items table with search and status filtering\n  - Pagination (50 items per page)\n  \n- `messages()`: Messages page with:\n  - Tab navigation\n  - Messages table with severity filtering\n  - Pagination\n  - Severity icons (Error/Warning/Notice badges)\n\n- Key helper methods:\n  - `loadMigration()`: Loads migration or throws 404, checks per-migration permissions\n  - `getMigrationStatus()`: Gets current migration status\n  - `getLastRunStats()`: Retrieves last run row from migrate_suite_run_log\n  - `buildImportedItemsSection()`: Complex method that:\n    - Queries migrate_map table with search/status filters\n    - Detects source and destination ID columns dynamically\n    - Attempts to link destination IDs to actual entities\n    - Builds paginated table\n  - `buildMessagesSection()`: Similar pattern for message table\n  - `buildItemFilterForm()` and `buildMessageFilterForm()`: Filter form builders\n  - `buildPager()`: Simple pager with Previous/Next navigation\n  - `buildEntityLink()`: Attempts to create links to destination entities\n  - `getRowStatusLabel()`, `getSeverityIcon()`: Status/severity formatting\n\n---\n\n### 6. ROUTING FILE\n**File: `/modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.routing.yml`**\n\nThree routes defined:\n\n```yaml\nmigrate_admin.dashboard:\n  path: '/admin/structure/migrate-suite'\n  defaults:\n    _controller: '\\Drupal\\migrate_admin\\Controller\\MigrationDashboardController::dashboard'\n    _title: 'Migration Dashboard'\n  requirements:\n    _permission: 'view migrate suite dashboard'\n\nmigrate_admin.migration_detail:\n  path: '/admin/structure/migrate-suite/{migration_id}'\n  defaults:\n    _controller: '\\Drupal\\migrate_admin\\Controller\\MigrationDetailController::detail'\n    _title: 'Migration Detail'\n  requirements:\n    _permission: 'view migrate suite dashboard'\n\nmigrate_admin.migration_messages:\n  path: '/admin/structure/migrate-suite/{migration_id}/messages'\n  defaults:\n    _controller: '\\Drupal\\migrate_admin\\Controller\\MigrationDetailController::messages'\n    _title: 'Migration Messages'\n  requirements:\n    _permission: 'view migrate suite dashboard'\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. PARENT SERVICES FILE\n**File: `/migrate_suite.services.yml`**\n\nRegisters three services:\n\n```yaml\nservices:\n  migrate_suite.map_query:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_suite\\Service\\MigrateMapQuery\n    arguments: ['@database', '@plugin.manager.migration']\n\n  migrate_suite.message_query:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_suite\\Service\\MigrateMessageQuery\n    arguments: ['@database']\n\n  migrate_suite.run_logger:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_suite\\EventSubscriber\\MigrateRunLogger\n    arguments: ['@database', '@datetime.time']\n    tags:\n      - { name: event_subscriber }\n```\n\n---\n\n### 8. MIGRATE PERMISSIONS SERVICES FILE\n**File: `/modules/migrate_permissions/migrate_permissions.services.yml`**\n\nSimple service registration:\n\n```yaml\nservices:\n  migrate_permissions.access_check:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_permissions\\MigrateAccessCheck\n```\n\n---\n\n### 9. CSS FILE\n**File: `/modules/migrate_admin/css/migrate_admin.css`**\n\nStyling for 84 lines covering:\n- **Badge styling**: Success (#28a745), Primary (#007bff), Warning (#ffc107), Error (#dc3545)\n- **Filter forms**: Flexbox layout with gap and wrapping\n- **Tabs**: Tab navigation styling with active state\n- **Pager**: Flexbox pager container with info text\n\n---\n\n### 10. LIBRARIES FILE\n**File: `/modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.libraries.yml`**\n\nSingle library definition:\n\n```yaml\ndashboard:\n  version: VERSION\n  css:\n    theme:\n      css/migrate_admin.css: {}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Integration Points\n\n1. **Permission System**: Both controllers conditionally use MigrateAccessCheck when migrate_permissions module is enabled\n2. **Database Tables**: \n   - `migrate_map_*` for item tracking\n   - `migrate_message_*` for run messages\n   - `migrate_suite_run_log` for run statistics\n3. **Dependency Injection**: Controllers use ContainerInterface to conditionally load MigrateAccessCheck service\n4. **Caching**: Dashboard caches by URL query args and migration_plugins tag\n5. **Service Dependencies**: All services use Drupal's core database and plugin manager services\n\nAll files are in `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite` as absolute paths in the directory structure shown."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ad1dfe5764073d328 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 46415\ntool_uses: 25\nduration_ms: 31844</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d40015d6-5dc4-4d37-b8ef-a7f6409020fa","uuid":"2bc9c70f-2f86-454a-a0f1-a8ac5ef9c52e","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Thoroughly explore the migrate_suite Drupal module codebase. I need to understand:\n\n1. The migrate_permissions submodule structure - read all files in modules/migrate_permissions/\n2. The dashboard controller - read modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDashboardController.php\n3. The detail controller - read modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDetailController.php\n4. The routing file - read modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.routing.yml\n5. The MigratePermissions class - read modules/migrate_permissions/src/MigratePermissions.php\n6. The MigrateAccessCheck class - read modules/migrate_permissions/src/MigrateAccessCheck.php\n7. The services files - read migrate_suite.services.yml and modules/migrate_permissions/migrate_permissions.services.yml\n8. The CSS file - read modules/migrate_admin/css/migrate_admin.css\n9. The migrate_admin libraries file - read modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.libraries.yml\n\nRead ALL of these files completely and return their full contents.","agentId":"ad1dfe5764073d328","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary of all the files I've read:\n\n## Complete Codebase Exploration Report\n\nI have thoroughly explored the migrate_suite Drupal module codebase and read all requested files. Here's the complete breakdown:\n\n### 1. MIGRATE_PERMISSIONS SUBMODULE STRUCTURE\n\n**All files in `/modules/migrate_permissions/`:**\n\n#### migrate_permissions.info.yml\n```yaml\nname: Migrate Permissions\ntype: module\ndescription: 'Provides granular per-migration permissions integrated with Drupal''s permission system.'\npackage: Migrate Suite\ncore_version_requirement: ^10.4 || ^11\ndependencies:\n  - migrate_suite:migrate_suite\n```\n\n#### migrate_permissions.module\n```php\n<?php\n\n/**\n * @file\n * Provides per-migration permissions for Migrate Suite.\n */\n```\n\n#### migrate_permissions.permissions.yml\n```yaml\npermission_callbacks:\n  - Drupal\\migrate_permissions\\MigratePermissions::permissions\n```\n\n#### migrate_permissions.services.yml\n```yaml\nservices:\n  migrate_permissions.access_check:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_permissions\\MigrateAccessCheck\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. MIPIGRATE PERMISSIONS CLASS\n**File: `/modules/migrate_permissions/src/MigratePermissions.php`**\n\nComplete PHP class that implements `ContainerInjectionInterface` and provides dynamic per-migration permissions. Key features:\n- Iterates through all migrations to generate permission definitions\n- Creates permission names using sanitized migration IDs (lowercase, alphanumeric + underscores)\n- Format: `view migration {safe_id}`\n- Each permission has a title and description\n- Gracefully handles exceptions when loading migrations\n\n---\n\n### 3. MIGRATE ACCESS CHECK CLASS\n**File: `/modules/migrate_permissions/src/MigrateAccessCheck.php`**\n\nSimple permission checker with one key method `canViewMigration()`:\n- Bypasses checks for users with 'administer migrations' or 'administer site configuration' permissions\n- Checks for per-migration view permission using sanitized migration ID\n- Returns boolean indicating whether user can view a specific migration\n\n---\n\n### 4. MIGRATION DASHBOARD CONTROLLER\n**File: `/modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDashboardController.php`**\n\nComprehensive controller (546 lines) with these key methods:\n- `dashboard()`: Main page builder that:\n  - Accepts search, status, and group filters via query parameters\n  - Applies per-migration view permissions if migrate_permissions module is enabled\n  - Groups migrations by their migration_group\n  - Builds filter form and migration group tables\n  - Caches results with migration_plugins tag\n  \n- Helper methods:\n  - `getMigrationStatus()`: Maps Drupal status labels to internal statuses (idle, importing, rolling_back, completed, failed)\n  - `getItemCounts()`: Queries migrate_map table for imported/failed/needs_update counts\n  - `getSourceCount()`: Gets source plugin item count\n  - `getLastRunTimestamp()`: Retrieves last run timestamp from migrate_suite_run_log\n  - `buildFilterForm()`: Creates HTML filter form with search, status, and group dropdowns\n  - `buildGroupTable()`: Creates details element with migration table for each group\n  - `buildStatusBadge()`: Creates colored badge spans\n\n---\n\n### 5. MIGRATION DETAIL CONTROLLER\n**File: `/modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDetailController.php`**\n\nLarge controller (912 lines) handling two main pages with these key methods:\n- `detail()`: Imported items page with:\n  - Summary section showing migration metadata\n  - Tab navigation between \"Imported Items\" and \"Messages\"\n  - Imported items table with search and status filtering\n  - Pagination (50 items per page)\n  \n- `messages()`: Messages page with:\n  - Tab navigation\n  - Messages table with severity filtering\n  - Pagination\n  - Severity icons (Error/Warning/Notice badges)\n\n- Key helper methods:\n  - `loadMigration()`: Loads migration or throws 404, checks per-migration permissions\n  - `getMigrationStatus()`: Gets current migration status\n  - `getLastRunStats()`: Retrieves last run row from migrate_suite_run_log\n  - `buildImportedItemsSection()`: Complex method that:\n    - Queries migrate_map table with search/status filters\n    - Detects source and destination ID columns dynamically\n    - Attempts to link destination IDs to actual entities\n    - Builds paginated table\n  - `buildMessagesSection()`: Similar pattern for message table\n  - `buildItemFilterForm()` and `buildMessageFilterForm()`: Filter form builders\n  - `buildPager()`: Simple pager with Previous/Next navigation\n  - `buildEntityLink()`: Attempts to create links to destination entities\n  - `getRowStatusLabel()`, `getSeverityIcon()`: Status/severity formatting\n\n---\n\n### 6. ROUTING FILE\n**File: `/modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.routing.yml`**\n\nThree routes defined:\n\n```yaml\nmigrate_admin.dashboard:\n  path: '/admin/structure/migrate-suite'\n  defaults:\n    _controller: '\\Drupal\\migrate_admin\\Controller\\MigrationDashboardController::dashboard'\n    _title: 'Migration Dashboard'\n  requirements:\n    _permission: 'view migrate suite dashboard'\n\nmigrate_admin.migration_detail:\n  path: '/admin/structure/migrate-suite/{migration_id}'\n  defaults:\n    _controller: '\\Drupal\\migrate_admin\\Controller\\MigrationDetailController::detail'\n    _title: 'Migration Detail'\n  requirements:\n    _permission: 'view migrate suite dashboard'\n\nmigrate_admin.migration_messages:\n  path: '/admin/structure/migrate-suite/{migration_id}/messages'\n  defaults:\n    _controller: '\\Drupal\\migrate_admin\\Controller\\MigrationDetailController::messages'\n    _title: 'Migration Messages'\n  requirements:\n    _permission: 'view migrate suite dashboard'\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. PARENT SERVICES FILE\n**File: `/migrate_suite.services.yml`**\n\nRegisters three services:\n\n```yaml\nservices:\n  migrate_suite.map_query:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_suite\\Service\\MigrateMapQuery\n    arguments: ['@database', '@plugin.manager.migration']\n\n  migrate_suite.message_query:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_suite\\Service\\MigrateMessageQuery\n    arguments: ['@database']\n\n  migrate_suite.run_logger:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_suite\\EventSubscriber\\MigrateRunLogger\n    arguments: ['@database', '@datetime.time']\n    tags:\n      - { name: event_subscriber }\n```\n\n---\n\n### 8. MIGRATE PERMISSIONS SERVICES FILE\n**File: `/modules/migrate_permissions/migrate_permissions.services.yml`**\n\nSimple service registration:\n\n```yaml\nservices:\n  migrate_permissions.access_check:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_permissions\\MigrateAccessCheck\n```\n\n---\n\n### 9. CSS FILE\n**File: `/modules/migrate_admin/css/migrate_admin.css`**\n\nStyling for 84 lines covering:\n- **Badge styling**: Success (#28a745), Primary (#007bff), Warning (#ffc107), Error (#dc3545)\n- **Filter forms**: Flexbox layout with gap and wrapping\n- **Tabs**: Tab navigation styling with active state\n- **Pager**: Flexbox pager container with info text\n\n---\n\n### 10. LIBRARIES FILE\n**File: `/modules/migrate_admin/migrate_admin.libraries.yml`**\n\nSingle library definition:\n\n```yaml\ndashboard:\n  version: VERSION\n  css:\n    theme:\n      css/migrate_admin.css: {}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Integration Points\n\n1. **Permission System**: Both controllers conditionally use MigrateAccessCheck when migrate_permissions module is enabled\n2. **Database Tables**: \n   - `migrate_map_*` for item tracking\n   - `migrate_message_*` for run messages\n   - `migrate_suite_run_log` for run statistics\n3. **Dependency Injection**: Controllers use ContainerInterface to conditionally load MigrateAccessCheck service\n4. **Caching**: Dashboard caches by URL query args and migration_plugins tag\n5. **Service Dependencies**: All services use Drupal's core database and plugin manager services\n\nAll files are in `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite` as absolute paths in the directory structure shown."}],"totalDurationMs":31844,"totalTokens":46415,"totalToolUseCount":25,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":512,"cache_read_input_tokens":43817,"output_tokens":2080,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":512},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
