{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019YJFcrDZDL554FTpbVgm12","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→<?php\n     2→\n     3→declare(strict_types=1);\n     4→\n     5→namespace Drupal\\migrate_admin\\Controller;\n     6→\n     7→use Drupal\\Core\\Controller\\ControllerBase;\n     8→use Drupal\\Core\\Database\\Connection;\n     9→use Drupal\\Core\\Datetime\\DateFormatterInterface;\n    10→use Drupal\\Core\\Url;\n    11→use Drupal\\migrate\\Plugin\\MigrationPluginManagerInterface;\n    12→use Drupal\\migrate_permissions\\MigrateAccessCheck;\n    13→use Symfony\\Component\\DependencyInjection\\ContainerInterface;\n    14→use Symfony\\Component\\HttpFoundation\\Request;\n    15→use Symfony\\Component\\HttpKernel\\Exception\\AccessDeniedHttpException;\n    16→use Symfony\\Component\\HttpKernel\\Exception\\NotFoundHttpException;\n    17→\n    18→/**\n    19→ * Controller for the migration detail page.\n    20→ */\n    21→class MigrationDetailController extends ControllerBase {\n    22→\n    23→  /**\n    24→   * Number of items per page.\n    25→   */\n    26→  protected const ITEMS_PER_PAGE = 50;\n    27→\n    28→  /**\n    29→   * Constructs a MigrationDetailController object.\n    30→   *\n    31→   * @param \\Drupal\\migrate\\Plugin\\MigrationPluginManagerInterface $migrationPluginManager\n    32→   *   The migration plugin manager.\n    33→   * @param \\Drupal\\Core\\Database\\Connection $database\n    34→   *   The database connection.\n    35→   * @param \\Drupal\\Core\\Datetime\\DateFormatterInterface $dateFormatter\n    36→   *   The date formatter service.\n    37→   */\n    38→  public function __construct(\n    39→    protected readonly MigrationPluginManagerInterface $migrationPluginManager,\n    40→    protected readonly Connection $database,\n    41→    protected readonly DateFormatterInterface $dateFormatter,\n    42→    protected readonly ?MigrateAccessCheck $migrateAccessCheck,\n    43→  ) {}\n    44→\n    45→  /**\n    46→   * {@inheritdoc}\n    47→   */\n    48→  public static function create(ContainerInterface $container): static {\n    49→    $migrateAccessCheck = $container->get('module_handler')->moduleExists('migrate_permissions')\n    50→      ? $container->get('migrate_permissions.access_check')\n    51→      : NULL;\n    52→\n    53→    return new static(\n    54→      $container->get('plugin.manager.migration'),\n    55→      $container->get('database'),\n    56→      $container->get('date.formatter'),\n    57→      $migrateAccessCheck,\n    58→    );\n    59→  }\n    60→\n    61→  /**\n    62→   * Builds the migration detail page.\n    63→   *\n    64→   * @param string $migration_id\n    65→   *   The migration plugin ID.\n    66→   * @param \\Symfony\\Component\\HttpFoundation\\Request $request\n    67→   *   The current request.\n    68→   *\n    69→   * @return array\n    70→   *   A render array.\n    71→   */\n    72→  public function detail(string $migration_id, Request $request): array {\n    73→    $migration = $this->loadMigration($migration_id);\n    74→\n    75→    $definition = $migration->getPluginDefinition();\n    76→    $group = $definition['migration_group'] ?? 'default';\n    77→    $sourcePlugin = $definition['source']['plugin'] ?? $this->t('Unknown');\n    78→    $destinationPlugin = $definition['destination']['plugin'] ?? $this->t('Unknown');\n    79→\n    80→    // Get status.\n    81→    $status = $this->getMigrationStatus($migration);\n    82→\n    83→    // Get last run stats.\n    84→    $lastRun = $this->getLastRunStats($migration_id);\n    85→\n    86→    // Build summary section.\n    87→    $build = [];\n    88→\n    89→    $build['summary'] = [\n    90→      '#type' => 'details',\n    91→      '#title' => $this->t('Summary'),\n    92→      '#open' => TRUE,\n    93→      'table' => [\n    94→        '#type' => 'table',\n    95→        '#rows' => [\n    96→          [$this->t('Migration'), $migration->label() ?: $migration_id],\n    97→          [$this->t('Group'), $group],\n    98→          [$this->t('Source plugin'), $sourcePlugin],\n    99→          [$this->t('Destination plugin'), $destinationPlugin],\n   100→          [$this->t('Status'), $this->buildStatusBadge($status)],"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01PnAFK2r5kSh8K8TwvF49xg","session_id":"47a3c04a-88ca-462e-9d23-1a6a80ee0429","uuid":"68b563e4-0205-41b4-81c8-7da90ead343a"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PnAFK2r5kSh8K8TwvF49xg","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile a comprehensive exploration report.\n\n## Comprehensive Codebase Structure Analysis for migrate_health Submodule\n\nBased on my thorough exploration of the codebase, here's everything you need to know to implement the migrate_health submodule:\n\n---\n\n## 1. SUBMODULE STRUCTURE PATTERN\n\nBoth existing submodules (migrate_admin and migrate_permissions) follow this consistent structure:\n\n### Directory Layout:\n```\nmodules/migrate_admin/\n├── css/\n│   └── migrate_admin.css\n├── src/\n│   ├── Controller/\n│   │   ├── MigrationDashboardController.php\n│   │   └── MigrationDetailController.php\n│   └── Form/\n│       ├── MigrationRunConfirmForm.php\n│       └── MigrationRollbackConfirmForm.php\n├── migrate_admin.info.yml\n├── migrate_admin.libraries.yml\n├── migrate_admin.links.menu.yml\n├── migrate_admin.module\n├── migrate_admin.permissions.yml\n└── migrate_admin.routing.yml\n\nmodules/migrate_permissions/\n├── css/\n│   └── migrate_permissions.css\n├── src/\n│   ├── Form/\n│   │   └── PermissionMatrixForm.php\n│   ├── MigrateAccessCheck.php\n│   └── MigratePermissions.php\n├── migrate_permissions.info.yml\n├── migrate_permissions.libraries.yml\n├── migrate_permissions.links.menu.yml\n├── migrate_permissions.module\n├── migrate_permissions.permissions.yml\n├── migrate_permissions.routing.yml\n└── migrate_permissions.services.yml\n```\n\n### Key Files to Create for migrate_health:\n- `migrate_health.info.yml` - Module metadata\n- `migrate_health.routing.yml` - Routes (if adding pages/services)\n- `migrate_health.services.yml` - Service definitions (if needed)\n- `migrate_health.permissions.yml` - Custom permissions (if needed)\n- `migrate_health.links.menu.yml` - Menu links (if adding UI)\n- `migrate_health.libraries.yml` - CSS/JS libraries (if needed)\n- `migrate_health.module` - Empty or hook implementations\n- `src/Service/` or `src/Controller/` - PHP classes\n- `css/` - Styling if needed\n\n---\n\n## 2. PARENT MODULE SERVICES (migrate_suite.services.yml)\n\n```yaml\nservices:\n  migrate_suite.map_query:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_suite\\Service\\MigrateMapQuery\n    arguments: ['@database', '@plugin.manager.migration']\n\n  migrate_suite.message_query:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_suite\\Service\\MigrateMessageQuery\n    arguments: ['@database']\n\n  migrate_suite.run_logger:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_suite\\EventSubscriber\\MigrateRunLogger\n    arguments: ['@database', '@datetime.time']\n    tags:\n      - { name: event_subscriber }\n```\n\n**Available for migrate_health to use:**\n- `@database` - Database connection\n- `@plugin.manager.migration` - Migration plugin manager\n- `@datetime.time` - Time service\n- Services from parent migrate_suite can be injected (map_query, message_query)\n\n---\n\n## 3. RUN_LOG TABLE SCHEMA (migrate_suite.install)\n\nThe migrate_health module will likely query this table:\n\n```php\n'migrate_suite_run_log' => [\n  'fields' => [\n    'id' => [type: 'serial', unsigned: TRUE, not null: TRUE],\n    'migration_id' => [type: 'varchar', length: 255, not null: TRUE],\n    'status' => [type: 'varchar', length: 32, not null: TRUE, default: 'idle'],\n    'started' => [type: 'int', not null: TRUE, default: 0],\n    'finished' => [type: 'int', not null: FALSE, default: NULL],\n    'items_processed' => [type: 'int', unsigned: TRUE, not null: TRUE, default: 0],\n    'items_created' => [type: 'int', unsigned: TRUE, not null: TRUE, default: 0],\n    'items_updated' => [type: 'int', unsigned: TRUE, not null: TRUE, default: 0],\n    'items_failed' => [type: 'int', unsigned: TRUE, not null: TRUE, default: 0],\n  ],\n  'primary key' => ['id'],\n  'indexes' => [\n    'migration_id' => ['migration_id'],\n    'status' => ['status'],\n  ],\n]\n```\n\n**Key metrics available:**\n- Run status (idle, running, completed, failed)\n- Items processed, created, updated, failed\n- Timestamps (started, finished)\n\n---\n\n## 4. MIGRATEMAPQUERY SERVICE (for item counts)\n\nLocation: `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/src/Service/MigrateMapQuery.php`\n\n**Key Methods:**\n\n```php\npublic function countItemsByStatus(string $migrationId): array\n// Returns: ['imported' => int, 'needs_update' => int, 'failed' => int]\n\npublic function lookupDestinationIds(string $migrationId, array $sourceIdValues): array\n// Returns destination IDs for source items\n\npublic function listImportedItems(string $migrationId, int $limit = 50, int $offset = 0): array\n// Returns paginated map table rows\n```\n\n**Map table status constants:**\n- `MigrateIdMapInterface::STATUS_IMPORTED` = 0\n- `MigrateIdMapInterface::STATUS_NEEDS_UPDATE` = 1\n- `MigrateIdMapInterface::STATUS_FAILED` = 2\n\n**Note:** The service queries tables named `migrate_map_{migrationId}` which are managed by Drupal's migrate system.\n\n---\n\n## 5. DASHBOARD INTEGRATION PATTERN (MigrationDashboardController)\n\nLocation: `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDashboardController.php`\n\n### Current Health Badge Implementation:\n```php\nprotected function buildStatusBadge(string $status): array|string {\n  $labels = [\n    'idle' => $this->t('Idle'),\n    'importing' => $this->t('Importing'),\n    'rolling_back' => $this->t('Rolling back'),\n    'completed' => $this->t('Completed'),\n    'failed' => $this->t('Failed'),\n  ];\n\n  $colors = [\n    'idle' => 'color--success',\n    'importing' => 'color--primary',\n    'rolling_back' => 'color--warning',\n    'completed' => 'color--success',\n    'failed' => 'color--error',\n  ];\n\n  return [\n    'data' => [\n      '#markup' => '<span class=\"badge ' . $colorClass . '\">' . $label . '</span>',\n    ],\n  ];\n}\n```\n\n### How to Add Health Badges:\n1. The controller iterates through migrations (line 87)\n2. For each migration, it calls helper methods:\n   - `getMigrationStatus()` - Gets current status\n   - `getItemCounts()` - Gets imported/failed counts from map table\n   - `getSourceCount()` - Gets source count\n   - `getLastRunTimestamp()` - Gets last run time\n3. Data is collected into `$groupedMigrations[$group][$migrationId]` array\n4. This data is then passed to `buildGroupTable()` which builds table rows\n5. Each row cell at index 2 contains the status badge (line 484)\n\n**To add a health badge column:**\n- Extend the data collection in the loop (lines 87-148)\n- Add your health metric to `$groupedMigrations[$group][$migrationId]`\n- Add a new column header in `buildGroupTable()` (line 515+)\n- Add a new cell in each row (line 502+)\n- Create a `buildHealthBadge()` similar to `buildStatusBadge()`\n\n---\n\n## 6. CSS STYLING PATTERNS\n\n### migrate_admin.css Badge Styling:\n```css\n.badge {\n  display: inline-block;\n  padding: 2px 8px;\n  border-radius: 3px;\n  font-size: 0.85em;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  color: #fff;\n}\n\n.badge.color--success { background-color: #28a745; }\n.badge.color--primary { background-color: #007bff; }\n.badge.color--warning { background-color: #ffc107; color: #333; }\n.badge.color--error { background-color: #dc3545; }\n```\n\n### migrate_permissions.css Table Styling:\n```css\n.migrate-permission-matrix { font-size: 0.9em; }\n.migrate-matrix-subheader td { text-align: center; font-weight: 600; }\n.migrate-matrix-group-header { background-color: #f0f0f0; font-weight: 700; }\n```\n\n### Dashboard Layout:\n```css\n.migrate-dashboard-filter-form {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 1em;\n  align-items: flex-end;\n  margin-bottom: 1.5em;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n}\n\n.migrate-detail-tabs {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 0;\n  margin-bottom: 1.5em;\n  border-bottom: 2px solid #ccc;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. MODULE METADATA EXAMPLES\n\n### migrate_admin.info.yml:\n```yaml\nname: Migrate Admin\ntype: module\ndescription: 'Migration dashboard with status overview and imported items list.'\npackage: Migration\ncore_version_requirement: ^10.4 || ^11\ndependencies:\n  - migrate_suite:migrate_suite\n```\n\n### migrate_permissions.info.yml:\n```yaml\nname: Migrate Permissions\ntype: module\ndescription: 'Provides granular per-migration permissions integrated with Drupal''s permission system.'\npackage: Migrate Suite\ncore_version_requirement: ^10.4 || ^11\ndependencies:\n  - migrate_suite:migrate_suite\n```\n\n**For migrate_health**, you would use:\n```yaml\nname: Migrate Health\ntype: module\ndescription: 'Provides health monitoring and badges for migrations.'\npackage: Migrate Suite\ncore_version_requirement: ^10.4 || ^11\ndependencies:\n  - migrate_suite:migrate_suite\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. ROUTING PATTERN\n\n### migrate_admin.routing.yml:\n```yaml\nmigrate_admin.dashboard:\n  path: '/admin/structure/migrate-suite'\n  defaults:\n    _controller: '\\Drupal\\migrate_admin\\Controller\\MigrationDashboardController::dashboard'\n    _title: 'Migration Dashboard'\n  requirements:\n    _permission: 'view migrate suite dashboard'\n\nmigrate_admin.migration_detail:\n  path: '/admin/structure/migrate-suite/{migration_id}'\n  defaults:\n    _controller: '\\Drupal\\migrate_admin\\Controller\\MigrationDetailController::detail'\n    _title: 'Migration Detail'\n  requirements:\n    _permission: 'view migrate suite dashboard'\n```\n\n### migrate_permissions.routing.yml:\n```yaml\nmigrate_permissions.permission_matrix:\n  path: '/admin/structure/migrate-suite/permissions'\n  defaults:\n    _form: '\\Drupal\\migrate_permissions\\Form\\PermissionMatrixForm'\n    _title: 'Migration Permissions'\n  requirements:\n    _permission: 'administer permissions'\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. LIBRARIES/ASSETS PATTERN\n\n### migrate_admin.libraries.yml:\n```yaml\ndashboard:\n  version: VERSION\n  css:\n    theme:\n      css/migrate_admin.css: {}\n```\n\n### migrate_permissions.libraries.yml:\n```yaml\nmatrix:\n  version: VERSION\n  css:\n    theme:\n      css/migrate_permissions.css: {}\n```\n\n**In controllers, attach libraries like:**\n```php\n$build['#attached'] = [\n  'library' => ['migrate_admin/dashboard'],\n];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. SERVICE DEFINITIONS PATTERN\n\n### migrate_permissions.services.yml:\n```yaml\nservices:\n  migrate_permissions.access_check:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_permissions\\MigrateAccessCheck\n```\n\n### For migrate_health, if you create a health analyzer service:\n```yaml\nservices:\n  migrate_health.analyzer:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_health\\Service\\MigrationHealthAnalyzer\n    arguments: ['@database', '@plugin.manager.migration', '@migrate_suite.map_query']\n```\n\n---\n\n## 11. EVENT SUBSCRIBER PATTERN (for real-time health tracking)\n\nThe parent module's MigrateRunLogger shows the pattern:\n\nLocation: `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/src/EventSubscriber/MigrateRunLogger.php`\n\n```php\npublic static function getSubscribedEvents(): array {\n  return [\n    MigrateEvents::PRE_IMPORT => ['onPreImport'],\n    MigrateEvents::POST_IMPORT => ['onPostImport'],\n    MigrateEvents::PRE_ROW_SAVE => ['onPreRowSave'],\n    MigrateEvents::POST_ROW_SAVE => ['onPostRowSave'],\n  ];\n}\n```\n\n**Available Migrate Events:**\n- `MigrateEvents::PRE_IMPORT` - Before migration starts\n- `MigrateEvents::POST_IMPORT` - After migration ends\n- `MigrateEvents::PRE_ROW_SAVE` - Before each row saves\n- `MigrateEvents::POST_ROW_SAVE` - After each row saves\n\nIf migrate_health needs to track health metrics during migration, it could subscribe to these events.\n\n---\n\n## 12. PERMISSION PATTERN\n\n### migrate_admin.permissions.yml:\n```yaml\nview migrate suite dashboard:\n  title: 'View Migrate Suite dashboard'\n  description: 'Access the migration dashboard and view migration status.'\n```\n\n### migrate_permissions.permissions.yml:\n```yaml\npermission_callbacks:\n  - Drupal\\migrate_permissions\\MigratePermissions::permissions\n```\n\n**For migrate_health**, you might add:\n```yaml\nview migrate health:\n  title: 'View migration health information'\n  description: 'Access migration health badges and statistics.'\n```\n\n---\n\n## 13. MENU LINKS PATTERN\n\n### migrate_admin.links.menu.yml:\n```yaml\nmigrate_admin.dashboard:\n  title: 'Migration Dashboard'\n  description: 'View and monitor migration status.'\n  route_name: migrate_admin.dashboard\n  parent: system.admin_structure\n  weight: 50\n```\n\n### migrate_permissions.links.menu.yml:\n```yaml\nmigrate_permissions.permission_matrix:\n  title: 'Migration Permissions'\n  description: 'Configure per-migration permissions for roles.'\n  route_name: migrate_permissions.permission_matrix\n  parent: system.admin_structure\n  weight: 51\n```\n\n---\n\n## 14. KEY DATA FLOW FOR HEALTH BADGES\n\nThe dashboard follows this flow:\n\n1. **Controller method called**: `MigrationDashboardController::dashboard(Request $request)`\n2. **Load all migrations**: `$migrations = $this->migrationPluginManager->createInstances([])`\n3. **For each migration, collect:**\n   - Migration ID and label\n   - Current status (from `migration->getStatusLabel()` or run_log table)\n   - Item counts (from migrate_map_* tables via `getItemCounts()`)\n   - Source count (from migration source plugin)\n   - Last run timestamp (from run_log table)\n4. **Filter based on search/status/group**\n5. **Group by migration_group**\n6. **Build render arrays** with status badges\n7. **Attach library** for CSS: `['#attached' => ['library' => ['migrate_admin/dashboard']]]`\n8. **Return render array** to Drupal for rendering\n\n**For health badges, insert at step 3 or 4:**\n- Query additional health metrics from run_log\n- Calculate health score/status\n- Add to groupedMigrations data structure\n- Build health badge in buildGroupTable()\n\n---\n\n## 15. INTERFACE PATTERNS\n\n### MigrateAccessCheck pattern (optional dependency):\nThe controllers check if migrate_permissions is enabled:\n```php\n$migrateAccessCheck = $container->get('module_handler')->moduleExists('migrate_permissions')\n  ? $container->get('migrate_permissions.access_check')\n  : NULL;\n```\n\nIf migrate_health needs conditional functionality based on other modules, follow this pattern.\n\n---\n\n## 16. DATABASE QUERY PATTERNS\n\n### From MigrationDashboardController:\n```php\n// Query run_log for migration status:\n$result = $this->database->select('migrate_suite_run_log', 'r')\n  ->fields('r', ['status'])\n  ->condition('migration_id', $migrationId)\n  ->orderBy('id', 'DESC')\n  ->range(0, 1)\n  ->execute()\n  ->fetchField();\n\n// Query map table for item counts:\n$results = $this->database->select($table, 'map')\n  ->fields('map', ['source_row_status'])\n  ->groupBy('source_row_status')\n  ->addExpression('COUNT(*)', 'count')\n  ->execute()\n  ->fetchAllKeyed();\n```\n\n**For migrate_health health calculations, you could:**\n- Get recent run history: `ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 10`\n- Calculate success rate: successful runs / total runs\n- Get failure counts: query run_log for status='failed'\n- Get average process time: `(finished - started) / items_processed`\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table\n\n| Aspect | Pattern | Location |\n|--------|---------|----------|\n| Info metadata | Dependency on migrate_suite | modules/*/..info.yml |\n| Services | Injected via DI container | modules/*/..services.yml |\n| Routes | RESTful paths under /admin/structure/migrate-suite | modules/*/..routing.yml |\n| Controllers | Extend ControllerBase, use create() pattern | modules/*/src/Controller/ |\n| Styling | Utility classes (badge, color--*) | modules/*/css/ |\n| Libraries | Attached via #attached['library'] | modules/*/..libraries.yml |\n| Permissions | Simple YAML or callback-based | modules/*/..permissions.yml |\n| Database | Query run_log and map_* tables | ..install file |\n| Services | MigrateMapQuery, MigrateMessageQuery available | migrate_suite.services.yml |\n\n---\n\nThis comprehensive analysis gives you all the patterns and details needed to implement migrate_health as a proper Drupal submodule that integrates seamlessly with the existing migrate_suite infrastructure."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a04a8302775504152 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 48355\ntool_uses: 38\nduration_ms: 74294</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47a3c04a-88ca-462e-9d23-1a6a80ee0429","uuid":"08973b5e-8ec3-4dc6-aeca-c09c9ce20713","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the codebase structure for implementing a \"migrate_health\" submodule. I need to understand:\n\n1. The existing submodule structure - look at modules/migrate_admin/ and modules/migrate_permissions/ for patterns (info.yml, routing, services, etc.)\n2. The parent module's migrate_suite.services.yml and what services exist\n3. The MigrationDashboardController.php to understand how to add health badges to the dashboard\n4. The migrate_suite.install file to understand the run_log table schema\n5. The MigrateMapQuery service to understand how to get item counts\n6. Any existing CSS files for badge styling\n\nThoroughness: very thorough. Read the full contents of these key files.","agentId":"a04a8302775504152","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile a comprehensive exploration report.\n\n## Comprehensive Codebase Structure Analysis for migrate_health Submodule\n\nBased on my thorough exploration of the codebase, here's everything you need to know to implement the migrate_health submodule:\n\n---\n\n## 1. SUBMODULE STRUCTURE PATTERN\n\nBoth existing submodules (migrate_admin and migrate_permissions) follow this consistent structure:\n\n### Directory Layout:\n```\nmodules/migrate_admin/\n├── css/\n│   └── migrate_admin.css\n├── src/\n│   ├── Controller/\n│   │   ├── MigrationDashboardController.php\n│   │   └── MigrationDetailController.php\n│   └── Form/\n│       ├── MigrationRunConfirmForm.php\n│       └── MigrationRollbackConfirmForm.php\n├── migrate_admin.info.yml\n├── migrate_admin.libraries.yml\n├── migrate_admin.links.menu.yml\n├── migrate_admin.module\n├── migrate_admin.permissions.yml\n└── migrate_admin.routing.yml\n\nmodules/migrate_permissions/\n├── css/\n│   └── migrate_permissions.css\n├── src/\n│   ├── Form/\n│   │   └── PermissionMatrixForm.php\n│   ├── MigrateAccessCheck.php\n│   └── MigratePermissions.php\n├── migrate_permissions.info.yml\n├── migrate_permissions.libraries.yml\n├── migrate_permissions.links.menu.yml\n├── migrate_permissions.module\n├── migrate_permissions.permissions.yml\n├── migrate_permissions.routing.yml\n└── migrate_permissions.services.yml\n```\n\n### Key Files to Create for migrate_health:\n- `migrate_health.info.yml` - Module metadata\n- `migrate_health.routing.yml` - Routes (if adding pages/services)\n- `migrate_health.services.yml` - Service definitions (if needed)\n- `migrate_health.permissions.yml` - Custom permissions (if needed)\n- `migrate_health.links.menu.yml` - Menu links (if adding UI)\n- `migrate_health.libraries.yml` - CSS/JS libraries (if needed)\n- `migrate_health.module` - Empty or hook implementations\n- `src/Service/` or `src/Controller/` - PHP classes\n- `css/` - Styling if needed\n\n---\n\n## 2. PARENT MODULE SERVICES (migrate_suite.services.yml)\n\n```yaml\nservices:\n  migrate_suite.map_query:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_suite\\Service\\MigrateMapQuery\n    arguments: ['@database', '@plugin.manager.migration']\n\n  migrate_suite.message_query:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_suite\\Service\\MigrateMessageQuery\n    arguments: ['@database']\n\n  migrate_suite.run_logger:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_suite\\EventSubscriber\\MigrateRunLogger\n    arguments: ['@database', '@datetime.time']\n    tags:\n      - { name: event_subscriber }\n```\n\n**Available for migrate_health to use:**\n- `@database` - Database connection\n- `@plugin.manager.migration` - Migration plugin manager\n- `@datetime.time` - Time service\n- Services from parent migrate_suite can be injected (map_query, message_query)\n\n---\n\n## 3. RUN_LOG TABLE SCHEMA (migrate_suite.install)\n\nThe migrate_health module will likely query this table:\n\n```php\n'migrate_suite_run_log' => [\n  'fields' => [\n    'id' => [type: 'serial', unsigned: TRUE, not null: TRUE],\n    'migration_id' => [type: 'varchar', length: 255, not null: TRUE],\n    'status' => [type: 'varchar', length: 32, not null: TRUE, default: 'idle'],\n    'started' => [type: 'int', not null: TRUE, default: 0],\n    'finished' => [type: 'int', not null: FALSE, default: NULL],\n    'items_processed' => [type: 'int', unsigned: TRUE, not null: TRUE, default: 0],\n    'items_created' => [type: 'int', unsigned: TRUE, not null: TRUE, default: 0],\n    'items_updated' => [type: 'int', unsigned: TRUE, not null: TRUE, default: 0],\n    'items_failed' => [type: 'int', unsigned: TRUE, not null: TRUE, default: 0],\n  ],\n  'primary key' => ['id'],\n  'indexes' => [\n    'migration_id' => ['migration_id'],\n    'status' => ['status'],\n  ],\n]\n```\n\n**Key metrics available:**\n- Run status (idle, running, completed, failed)\n- Items processed, created, updated, failed\n- Timestamps (started, finished)\n\n---\n\n## 4. MIGRATEMAPQUERY SERVICE (for item counts)\n\nLocation: `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/src/Service/MigrateMapQuery.php`\n\n**Key Methods:**\n\n```php\npublic function countItemsByStatus(string $migrationId): array\n// Returns: ['imported' => int, 'needs_update' => int, 'failed' => int]\n\npublic function lookupDestinationIds(string $migrationId, array $sourceIdValues): array\n// Returns destination IDs for source items\n\npublic function listImportedItems(string $migrationId, int $limit = 50, int $offset = 0): array\n// Returns paginated map table rows\n```\n\n**Map table status constants:**\n- `MigrateIdMapInterface::STATUS_IMPORTED` = 0\n- `MigrateIdMapInterface::STATUS_NEEDS_UPDATE` = 1\n- `MigrateIdMapInterface::STATUS_FAILED` = 2\n\n**Note:** The service queries tables named `migrate_map_{migrationId}` which are managed by Drupal's migrate system.\n\n---\n\n## 5. DASHBOARD INTEGRATION PATTERN (MigrationDashboardController)\n\nLocation: `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDashboardController.php`\n\n### Current Health Badge Implementation:\n```php\nprotected function buildStatusBadge(string $status): array|string {\n  $labels = [\n    'idle' => $this->t('Idle'),\n    'importing' => $this->t('Importing'),\n    'rolling_back' => $this->t('Rolling back'),\n    'completed' => $this->t('Completed'),\n    'failed' => $this->t('Failed'),\n  ];\n\n  $colors = [\n    'idle' => 'color--success',\n    'importing' => 'color--primary',\n    'rolling_back' => 'color--warning',\n    'completed' => 'color--success',\n    'failed' => 'color--error',\n  ];\n\n  return [\n    'data' => [\n      '#markup' => '<span class=\"badge ' . $colorClass . '\">' . $label . '</span>',\n    ],\n  ];\n}\n```\n\n### How to Add Health Badges:\n1. The controller iterates through migrations (line 87)\n2. For each migration, it calls helper methods:\n   - `getMigrationStatus()` - Gets current status\n   - `getItemCounts()` - Gets imported/failed counts from map table\n   - `getSourceCount()` - Gets source count\n   - `getLastRunTimestamp()` - Gets last run time\n3. Data is collected into `$groupedMigrations[$group][$migrationId]` array\n4. This data is then passed to `buildGroupTable()` which builds table rows\n5. Each row cell at index 2 contains the status badge (line 484)\n\n**To add a health badge column:**\n- Extend the data collection in the loop (lines 87-148)\n- Add your health metric to `$groupedMigrations[$group][$migrationId]`\n- Add a new column header in `buildGroupTable()` (line 515+)\n- Add a new cell in each row (line 502+)\n- Create a `buildHealthBadge()` similar to `buildStatusBadge()`\n\n---\n\n## 6. CSS STYLING PATTERNS\n\n### migrate_admin.css Badge Styling:\n```css\n.badge {\n  display: inline-block;\n  padding: 2px 8px;\n  border-radius: 3px;\n  font-size: 0.85em;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  color: #fff;\n}\n\n.badge.color--success { background-color: #28a745; }\n.badge.color--primary { background-color: #007bff; }\n.badge.color--warning { background-color: #ffc107; color: #333; }\n.badge.color--error { background-color: #dc3545; }\n```\n\n### migrate_permissions.css Table Styling:\n```css\n.migrate-permission-matrix { font-size: 0.9em; }\n.migrate-matrix-subheader td { text-align: center; font-weight: 600; }\n.migrate-matrix-group-header { background-color: #f0f0f0; font-weight: 700; }\n```\n\n### Dashboard Layout:\n```css\n.migrate-dashboard-filter-form {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 1em;\n  align-items: flex-end;\n  margin-bottom: 1.5em;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n}\n\n.migrate-detail-tabs {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 0;\n  margin-bottom: 1.5em;\n  border-bottom: 2px solid #ccc;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. MODULE METADATA EXAMPLES\n\n### migrate_admin.info.yml:\n```yaml\nname: Migrate Admin\ntype: module\ndescription: 'Migration dashboard with status overview and imported items list.'\npackage: Migration\ncore_version_requirement: ^10.4 || ^11\ndependencies:\n  - migrate_suite:migrate_suite\n```\n\n### migrate_permissions.info.yml:\n```yaml\nname: Migrate Permissions\ntype: module\ndescription: 'Provides granular per-migration permissions integrated with Drupal''s permission system.'\npackage: Migrate Suite\ncore_version_requirement: ^10.4 || ^11\ndependencies:\n  - migrate_suite:migrate_suite\n```\n\n**For migrate_health**, you would use:\n```yaml\nname: Migrate Health\ntype: module\ndescription: 'Provides health monitoring and badges for migrations.'\npackage: Migrate Suite\ncore_version_requirement: ^10.4 || ^11\ndependencies:\n  - migrate_suite:migrate_suite\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. ROUTING PATTERN\n\n### migrate_admin.routing.yml:\n```yaml\nmigrate_admin.dashboard:\n  path: '/admin/structure/migrate-suite'\n  defaults:\n    _controller: '\\Drupal\\migrate_admin\\Controller\\MigrationDashboardController::dashboard'\n    _title: 'Migration Dashboard'\n  requirements:\n    _permission: 'view migrate suite dashboard'\n\nmigrate_admin.migration_detail:\n  path: '/admin/structure/migrate-suite/{migration_id}'\n  defaults:\n    _controller: '\\Drupal\\migrate_admin\\Controller\\MigrationDetailController::detail'\n    _title: 'Migration Detail'\n  requirements:\n    _permission: 'view migrate suite dashboard'\n```\n\n### migrate_permissions.routing.yml:\n```yaml\nmigrate_permissions.permission_matrix:\n  path: '/admin/structure/migrate-suite/permissions'\n  defaults:\n    _form: '\\Drupal\\migrate_permissions\\Form\\PermissionMatrixForm'\n    _title: 'Migration Permissions'\n  requirements:\n    _permission: 'administer permissions'\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. LIBRARIES/ASSETS PATTERN\n\n### migrate_admin.libraries.yml:\n```yaml\ndashboard:\n  version: VERSION\n  css:\n    theme:\n      css/migrate_admin.css: {}\n```\n\n### migrate_permissions.libraries.yml:\n```yaml\nmatrix:\n  version: VERSION\n  css:\n    theme:\n      css/migrate_permissions.css: {}\n```\n\n**In controllers, attach libraries like:**\n```php\n$build['#attached'] = [\n  'library' => ['migrate_admin/dashboard'],\n];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. SERVICE DEFINITIONS PATTERN\n\n### migrate_permissions.services.yml:\n```yaml\nservices:\n  migrate_permissions.access_check:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_permissions\\MigrateAccessCheck\n```\n\n### For migrate_health, if you create a health analyzer service:\n```yaml\nservices:\n  migrate_health.analyzer:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_health\\Service\\MigrationHealthAnalyzer\n    arguments: ['@database', '@plugin.manager.migration', '@migrate_suite.map_query']\n```\n\n---\n\n## 11. EVENT SUBSCRIBER PATTERN (for real-time health tracking)\n\nThe parent module's MigrateRunLogger shows the pattern:\n\nLocation: `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/src/EventSubscriber/MigrateRunLogger.php`\n\n```php\npublic static function getSubscribedEvents(): array {\n  return [\n    MigrateEvents::PRE_IMPORT => ['onPreImport'],\n    MigrateEvents::POST_IMPORT => ['onPostImport'],\n    MigrateEvents::PRE_ROW_SAVE => ['onPreRowSave'],\n    MigrateEvents::POST_ROW_SAVE => ['onPostRowSave'],\n  ];\n}\n```\n\n**Available Migrate Events:**\n- `MigrateEvents::PRE_IMPORT` - Before migration starts\n- `MigrateEvents::POST_IMPORT` - After migration ends\n- `MigrateEvents::PRE_ROW_SAVE` - Before each row saves\n- `MigrateEvents::POST_ROW_SAVE` - After each row saves\n\nIf migrate_health needs to track health metrics during migration, it could subscribe to these events.\n\n---\n\n## 12. PERMISSION PATTERN\n\n### migrate_admin.permissions.yml:\n```yaml\nview migrate suite dashboard:\n  title: 'View Migrate Suite dashboard'\n  description: 'Access the migration dashboard and view migration status.'\n```\n\n### migrate_permissions.permissions.yml:\n```yaml\npermission_callbacks:\n  - Drupal\\migrate_permissions\\MigratePermissions::permissions\n```\n\n**For migrate_health**, you might add:\n```yaml\nview migrate health:\n  title: 'View migration health information'\n  description: 'Access migration health badges and statistics.'\n```\n\n---\n\n## 13. MENU LINKS PATTERN\n\n### migrate_admin.links.menu.yml:\n```yaml\nmigrate_admin.dashboard:\n  title: 'Migration Dashboard'\n  description: 'View and monitor migration status.'\n  route_name: migrate_admin.dashboard\n  parent: system.admin_structure\n  weight: 50\n```\n\n### migrate_permissions.links.menu.yml:\n```yaml\nmigrate_permissions.permission_matrix:\n  title: 'Migration Permissions'\n  description: 'Configure per-migration permissions for roles.'\n  route_name: migrate_permissions.permission_matrix\n  parent: system.admin_structure\n  weight: 51\n```\n\n---\n\n## 14. KEY DATA FLOW FOR HEALTH BADGES\n\nThe dashboard follows this flow:\n\n1. **Controller method called**: `MigrationDashboardController::dashboard(Request $request)`\n2. **Load all migrations**: `$migrations = $this->migrationPluginManager->createInstances([])`\n3. **For each migration, collect:**\n   - Migration ID and label\n   - Current status (from `migration->getStatusLabel()` or run_log table)\n   - Item counts (from migrate_map_* tables via `getItemCounts()`)\n   - Source count (from migration source plugin)\n   - Last run timestamp (from run_log table)\n4. **Filter based on search/status/group**\n5. **Group by migration_group**\n6. **Build render arrays** with status badges\n7. **Attach library** for CSS: `['#attached' => ['library' => ['migrate_admin/dashboard']]]`\n8. **Return render array** to Drupal for rendering\n\n**For health badges, insert at step 3 or 4:**\n- Query additional health metrics from run_log\n- Calculate health score/status\n- Add to groupedMigrations data structure\n- Build health badge in buildGroupTable()\n\n---\n\n## 15. INTERFACE PATTERNS\n\n### MigrateAccessCheck pattern (optional dependency):\nThe controllers check if migrate_permissions is enabled:\n```php\n$migrateAccessCheck = $container->get('module_handler')->moduleExists('migrate_permissions')\n  ? $container->get('migrate_permissions.access_check')\n  : NULL;\n```\n\nIf migrate_health needs conditional functionality based on other modules, follow this pattern.\n\n---\n\n## 16. DATABASE QUERY PATTERNS\n\n### From MigrationDashboardController:\n```php\n// Query run_log for migration status:\n$result = $this->database->select('migrate_suite_run_log', 'r')\n  ->fields('r', ['status'])\n  ->condition('migration_id', $migrationId)\n  ->orderBy('id', 'DESC')\n  ->range(0, 1)\n  ->execute()\n  ->fetchField();\n\n// Query map table for item counts:\n$results = $this->database->select($table, 'map')\n  ->fields('map', ['source_row_status'])\n  ->groupBy('source_row_status')\n  ->addExpression('COUNT(*)', 'count')\n  ->execute()\n  ->fetchAllKeyed();\n```\n\n**For migrate_health health calculations, you could:**\n- Get recent run history: `ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 10`\n- Calculate success rate: successful runs / total runs\n- Get failure counts: query run_log for status='failed'\n- Get average process time: `(finished - started) / items_processed`\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table\n\n| Aspect | Pattern | Location |\n|--------|---------|----------|\n| Info metadata | Dependency on migrate_suite | modules/*/..info.yml |\n| Services | Injected via DI container | modules/*/..services.yml |\n| Routes | RESTful paths under /admin/structure/migrate-suite | modules/*/..routing.yml |\n| Controllers | Extend ControllerBase, use create() pattern | modules/*/src/Controller/ |\n| Styling | Utility classes (badge, color--*) | modules/*/css/ |\n| Libraries | Attached via #attached['library'] | modules/*/..libraries.yml |\n| Permissions | Simple YAML or callback-based | modules/*/..permissions.yml |\n| Database | Query run_log and map_* tables | ..install file |\n| Services | MigrateMapQuery, MigrateMessageQuery available | migrate_suite.services.yml |\n\n---\n\nThis comprehensive analysis gives you all the patterns and details needed to implement migrate_health as a proper Drupal submodule that integrates seamlessly with the existing migrate_suite infrastructure."}],"totalDurationMs":74294,"totalTokens":48355,"totalToolUseCount":38,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1446,"cache_read_input_tokens":42208,"output_tokens":4699,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1446},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
