{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DNim5Njm8ZKP8ZXxuv36F4","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→{\n     2→  \"project\": \"Migrate Suite\",\n     3→  \"description\": \"Migrate Suite is a Drupal 10.4+ / 11.x module that provides an administration dashboard for managing and monitoring migrations. It fills a major gap in the Drupal migration ecosystem: once migrations are configured, there is no editor-friendly way to monitor their status, inspect migrated content, or control access per migration. The core Migrate module and Migrate Tools provide Drush commands and a minimal admin page, but site managers, content leads, and non-developer admins are left without visibility. Migrate Suite is a parent module with four independently installable submodules: migrate_admin (Migration dashboard with status overview and imported items list), migrate_source_field (Content provenance meta field and original source link field on migrated entities), migrate_permissions (Granular per-migration permissions integrated with Drupal's permission system), and migrate_health (Health badges, stale detection, and failed item tracking). This PRD covers Phase 1 (MVP) only.\",\n     4→  \"userStories\": [\n     5→    {\n     6→      \"id\": \"US-001\",\n     7→      \"title\": \"Set up shared services in migrate_suite parent module\",\n     8→      \"description\": \"As a developer, I need shared services in the parent module so that all submodules can query migration map/message tables and access run history without duplicating code.\",\n     9→      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    10→        \"migrate_suite.info.yml declares the module with dependency on core migrate\",\n    11→        \"MigrateMapQuery service exists that can: look up destination IDs by source ID, list all imported items for a migration, count items by status (imported/failed)\",\n    12→        \"MigrateMessageQuery service exists that can: fetch messages for a specific migration, fetch messages for a specific source ID within a migration\",\n    13→        \"Database schema defines migrate_suite_run_log table with columns: id, migration_id, status (idle/running/completed/failed), started, finished, items_processed, items_created, items_updated, items_failed\",\n    14→        \"Event subscriber listens to MigrateEvents::PRE_IMPORT, POST_IMPORT, PRE_ROW_SAVE, POST_ROW_SAVE and logs run data to migrate_suite_run_log\",\n    15→        \"All services are registered in migrate_suite.services.yml\",\n    16→        \"Module installs and uninstalls cleanly (schema install/uninstall hooks work)\",\n    17→        \"PHPStan/phpcs passes at Drupal coding standards\"\n    18→      ],\n    19→      \"priority\": 1,\n    20→      \"passes\": true\n    21→    },\n    22→    {\n    23→      \"id\": \"US-002\",\n    24→      \"title\": \"Migration overview dashboard page\",\n    25→      \"description\": \"As a site administrator, I want a dashboard listing all migrations with their current status so that I can monitor migration progress without using Drush.\",\n    26→      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    27→        \"Route at /admin/structure/migrate-suite with title \\\"Migration Dashboard\\\"\",\n    28→        \"Page lists all migration plugin instances with columns: label, migration group, status (idle/importing/rolling back/completed/failed), total source count, imported count, failed count, last run timestamp\",\n    29→        \"Status is displayed with a colored badge: green (completed/idle), blue (importing), red (failed), yellow (rolling back)\",\n    30→        \"Migrations are grouped by migration group with collapsible sections\",\n    31→        \"Filter form at top: text search (migration ID/label), status dropdown, migration group dropdown\",\n    32→        \"Each migration row links to a detail page (US-003)\",\n    33→        \"Page uses Drupal's admin theme and standard table formatting\",\n    34→        \"Empty state message shown when no migrations exist\",\n    35→        \"Page permission: view migrate suite dashboard (provided by migrate_admin)\"\n    36→      ],\n    37→      \"priority\": 2,\n    38→      \"passes\": true\n    39→    },\n    40→    {\n    41→      \"id\": \"US-003\",\n    42→      \"title\": \"Migration detail page with imported items\",\n    43→      \"description\": \"As a content lead, I want to see all entities imported by a specific migration so that I can verify content was migrated correctly.\",\n    44→      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    45→        \"Route at /admin/structure/migrate-suite/{migration_id} showing migration detail\",\n    46→        \"Summary section: migration label, group, source plugin, destination plugin, status, last run stats (from migrate_suite_run_log)\",\n    47→        \"Imported items table sourced from migrate_map_{migration_id} with columns: source ID(s), destination entity (linked to entity view), status (source_row_status: imported/needs update), last import timestamp (from map table last_imported column)\",\n    48→        \"Pager: 50 items per page\",\n    49→        \"Filter: text search on source ID, status dropdown (imported/needs update/failed)\",\n    50→        \"Migration messages tab showing messages from migrate_message_{migration_id} with columns: source ID(s), severity (icon), message text\",\n    51→        \"Messages filterable by severity (notice/warning/error)\",\n    52→        \"Uses same permission as dashboard: view migrate suite dashboard\"\n    53→      ],\n    54→      \"priority\": 3,\n    55→      \"passes\": true\n    56→    },\n    57→    {\n    58→      \"id\": \"US-004\",\n    59→      \"title\": \"Per-migration view permissions\",\n    60→      \"description\": \"As a site administrator, I want to control which roles can view specific migrations so that content leads only see migrations relevant to them.\",\n    61→      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    62→        \"migrate_permissions.info.yml declares the submodule with dependency on migrate_suite\",\n    63→        \"Module dynamically generates permissions in a permission callback: view migration {migration_id} for each migration plugin instance\",\n    64→        \"Permissions appear in Drupal's standard permissions page (/admin/people/permissions) under a \\\"Migrate Suite\\\" group\",\n    65→        \"Dashboard (US-002) filters the migration list based on the user's per-migration view permissions\",\n    66→        \"Detail page (US-003) checks per-migration view permission before displaying\",\n    67→        \"A user with view migrate suite dashboard permission but without any per-migration permissions sees an empty dashboard with a help message\",\n    68→        \"A user with administer migrations (from migrate_tools) or administer site configuration bypasses per-migration checks\",\n    69→        \"Permission names are derived from the migration plugin ID (machine-safe)\"\n    70→      ],\n    71→      \"priority\": 4,\n    72→      \"passes\": true\n    73→    },\n    74→    {\n    75→      \"id\": \"US-005\",\n    76→      \"title\": \"Per-migration run permissions\",\n    77→      \"description\": \"As a site administrator, I want to control which roles can execute or rollback specific migrations so that only authorized users can trigger imports.\",\n    78→      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    79→        \"Dynamic permissions generated: run migration {migration_id} and rollback migration {migration_id} for each migration\",\n    80→        \"Dashboard row shows \\\"Run\\\" and \\\"Rollback\\\" action buttons only if user has the corresponding permission\",\n    81→        \"Run action triggers a batch import of the migration and redirects to a batch progress page\",\n    82→        \"Rollback action triggers a batch rollback and redirects to a batch progress page\",\n    83→        \"Confirmation form shown before run/rollback with migration label and item count\",\n    84→        \"administer migrations permission bypasses per-migration run/rollback checks\",\n    85→        \"Actions respect migration dependencies (warn if dependent migrations haven't run)\"\n    86→      ],\n    87→      \"priority\": 5,\n    88→      \"passes\": true\n    89→    },\n    90→    {\n    91→      \"id\": \"US-006\",\n    92→      \"title\": \"Permission matrix UI\",\n    93→      \"description\": \"As a site administrator, I want a matrix view of migration permissions so that I can quickly see and configure which roles have access to which migrations.\",\n    94→      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    95→        \"Route at /admin/structure/migrate-suite/permissions with title \\\"Migration Permissions\\\"\",\n    96→        \"Matrix table: rows = migrations (grouped by migration group), columns = roles\",\n    97→        \"Each cell shows checkboxes for: view, run, rollback\",\n    98→        \"Form saves permissions via Drupal's user_role_grant_permissions / user_role_revoke_permissions API\",\n    99→        \"Matrix is filterable by migration group\",\n   100→        \"Requires administer permissions permission to access\",\n   101→        \"Changes are logged to watchdog\"\n   102→      ],\n   103→      \"priority\": 6,\n   104→      \"passes\": true\n   105→    },\n   106→    {\n   107→      \"id\": \"US-007\",\n   108→      \"title\": \"Migration health indicators\",\n   109→      \"description\": \"As a site administrator, I want to see at-a-glance health badges on each migration so that I can identify problems quickly.\",\n   110→      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n   111→        \"migrate_health.info.yml declares the submodule with dependency on migrate_suite\",\n   112→        \"Each migration on the dashboard shows a health badge: healthy (green), stale (yellow), failing (red)\",\n   113→        \"Healthy: migration has run within configured threshold AND failure rate is below configured threshold\",\n   114→        \"Stale: migration has not run within the configured \\\"stale after X days\\\" threshold (default: 7 days)\",\n   115→        \"Failing: migration's failure rate (failed items / total items) exceeds configured threshold (default: 5%)\",\n   116→        \"Health thresholds configurable via settings form at /admin/structure/migrate-suite/settings\",\n   117→        \"Settings form fields: stale threshold (days, default 7), failure rate threshold (percentage, default 5)\",\n   118→        \"Health is computed on dashboard load from migrate_suite_run_log and map table data (no separate cron task in MVP)\",\n   119→        \"Aggregate health summary at top of dashboard: \\\"X healthy, Y stale, Z failing\\\"\"\n   120→      ],\n   121→      \"priority\": 7,\n   122→      \"passes\": true\n   123→    },\n   124→    {\n   125→      \"id\": \"US-008\",\n   126→      \"title\": \"Failed item tracking\",\n   127→      \"description\": \"As a site administrator, I want to see which items failed to import with their error details so that I can take corrective action.\",\n   128→      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n   129→        \"Migration detail page (US-003) shows a \\\"Failed Items\\\" tab\",\n   130→        \"Tab lists items from migrate_map_{migration_id} where source_row_status = 2 (MigrateIdMapInterface::STATUS_FAILED)\",\n   131→        \"Columns: source ID(s), error message (from migrate_message_{migration_id}), last attempt timestamp\",\n   132→        \"Failed item count shown as a badge on the tab header\",\n   133→        \"Filter by source ID text search\",\n   134→        \"Pager: 50 items per page\",\n   135→        \"\\\"Reset status\\\" bulk action to mark selected failed items for retry (sets source_row_status back to 0)\",\n   136→        \"Reset action requires run migration {migration_id} permission (from migrate_permissions, or administer migrations if migrate_permissions is not installed)\"\n   137→      ],\n   138→      \"priority\": 8,\n   139→      \"passes\": false\n   140→    },\n   141→    {\n   142→      \"id\": \"US-009\",\n   143→      \"title\": \"Content provenance pseudo-field on migrated entities\",\n   144→      \"description\": \"As a content editor, I want to see migration provenance information on entity edit/view pages so that I can tell where content came from and when it was imported.\",\n   145→      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n   146→        \"migrate_source_field.info.yml declares the submodule with dependency on migrate_suite\",\n   147→        \"Module implements hook_entity_extra_field_info() to register a \\\"Migration provenance\\\" pseudo-field on node entities\",\n   148→        \"Pseudo-field is configurable per content type via \\\"Manage display\\\" (can be shown/hidden, reordered)\",\n   149→        \"When displayed, shows a fieldset with: migration label (linked to detail page if user has permission), import date (from map table last_imported), source ID(s)\",\n   150→        \"If entity is not found in any migrate_map_* table, pseudo-field is hidden (no empty fieldset)\",\n   151→        \"Provenance data is computed at render time by querying map tables (not stored redundantly)\",\n   152→        \"Results are cached per entity with appropriate cache tags (invalidated on migration run)\",\n   153→        \"Works on both entity canonical view and edit form\"\n   154→      ],\n   155→      \"priority\": 9,\n   156→      \"passes\": false\n   157→    },\n   158→    {\n   159→      \"id\": \"US-010\",\n   160→      \"title\": \"Original source link field\",\n   161→      \"description\": \"As a content editor, I want a link back to the original content on the source platform so that I can compare migrated content with the original.\",\n   162→      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n   163→        \"Configurable source URL pattern per migration via settings form, supporting a [source_id] token (e.g., https://old-site.com/node/[source_id])\",\n   164→        \"Settings stored in migrate_suite.settings config, keyed by migration ID\",\n   165→        \"Source link displayed within the provenance pseudo-field (US-009) as a clickable URL\",\n   166→        \"Link opens in a new tab (target=\\\"_blank\\\" with rel=\\\"noopener\\\")\",\n   167→        \"If no URL pattern is configured for a migration, the source link row is omitted (not shown as empty)\",\n   168→        \"URL pattern configuration form accessible at /admin/structure/migrate-suite/settings/source-links\",\n   169→        \"Form lists all migrations with a text field for each URL pattern\",\n   170→        \"Token replacement handles multiple source IDs (composite keys) by joining with /\"\n   171→      ],\n   172→      \"priority\": 10,\n   173→      \"passes\": false\n   174→    }\n   175→  ]\n   176→}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"804c2cf8-5541-47a7-a331-3655bdfe0e70","uuid":"929459e7-2ab6-4d72-a608-82841ba00e8d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/.chief/prds/main/prd.json","content":"{\n  \"project\": \"Migrate Suite\",\n  \"description\": \"Migrate Suite is a Drupal 10.4+ / 11.x module that provides an administration dashboard for managing and monitoring migrations. It fills a major gap in the Drupal migration ecosystem: once migrations are configured, there is no editor-friendly way to monitor their status, inspect migrated content, or control access per migration. The core Migrate module and Migrate Tools provide Drush commands and a minimal admin page, but site managers, content leads, and non-developer admins are left without visibility. Migrate Suite is a parent module with four independently installable submodules: migrate_admin (Migration dashboard with status overview and imported items list), migrate_source_field (Content provenance meta field and original source link field on migrated entities), migrate_permissions (Granular per-migration permissions integrated with Drupal's permission system), and migrate_health (Health badges, stale detection, and failed item tracking). This PRD covers Phase 1 (MVP) only.\",\n  \"userStories\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-001\",\n      \"title\": \"Set up shared services in migrate_suite parent module\",\n      \"description\": \"As a developer, I need shared services in the parent module so that all submodules can query migration map/message tables and access run history without duplicating code.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"migrate_suite.info.yml declares the module with dependency on core migrate\",\n        \"MigrateMapQuery service exists that can: look up destination IDs by source ID, list all imported items for a migration, count items by status (imported/failed)\",\n        \"MigrateMessageQuery service exists that can: fetch messages for a specific migration, fetch messages for a specific source ID within a migration\",\n        \"Database schema defines migrate_suite_run_log table with columns: id, migration_id, status (idle/running/completed/failed), started, finished, items_processed, items_created, items_updated, items_failed\",\n        \"Event subscriber listens to MigrateEvents::PRE_IMPORT, POST_IMPORT, PRE_ROW_SAVE, POST_ROW_SAVE and logs run data to migrate_suite_run_log\",\n        \"All services are registered in migrate_suite.services.yml\",\n        \"Module installs and uninstalls cleanly (schema install/uninstall hooks work)\",\n        \"PHPStan/phpcs passes at Drupal coding standards\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"passes\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-002\",\n      \"title\": \"Migration overview dashboard page\",\n      \"description\": \"As a site administrator, I want a dashboard listing all migrations with their current status so that I can monitor migration progress without using Drush.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Route at /admin/structure/migrate-suite with title \\\"Migration Dashboard\\\"\",\n        \"Page lists all migration plugin instances with columns: label, migration group, status (idle/importing/rolling back/completed/failed), total source count, imported count, failed count, last run timestamp\",\n        \"Status is displayed with a colored badge: green (completed/idle), blue (importing), red (failed), yellow (rolling back)\",\n        \"Migrations are grouped by migration group with collapsible sections\",\n        \"Filter form at top: text search (migration ID/label), status dropdown, migration group dropdown\",\n        \"Each migration row links to a detail page (US-003)\",\n        \"Page uses Drupal's admin theme and standard table formatting\",\n        \"Empty state message shown when no migrations exist\",\n        \"Page permission: view migrate suite dashboard (provided by migrate_admin)\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"passes\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-003\",\n      \"title\": \"Migration detail page with imported items\",\n      \"description\": \"As a content lead, I want to see all entities imported by a specific migration so that I can verify content was migrated correctly.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Route at /admin/structure/migrate-suite/{migration_id} showing migration detail\",\n        \"Summary section: migration label, group, source plugin, destination plugin, status, last run stats (from migrate_suite_run_log)\",\n        \"Imported items table sourced from migrate_map_{migration_id} with columns: source ID(s), destination entity (linked to entity view), status (source_row_status: imported/needs update), last import timestamp (from map table last_imported column)\",\n        \"Pager: 50 items per page\",\n        \"Filter: text search on source ID, status dropdown (imported/needs update/failed)\",\n        \"Migration messages tab showing messages from migrate_message_{migration_id} with columns: source ID(s), severity (icon), message text\",\n        \"Messages filterable by severity (notice/warning/error)\",\n        \"Uses same permission as dashboard: view migrate suite dashboard\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 3,\n      \"passes\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-004\",\n      \"title\": \"Per-migration view permissions\",\n      \"description\": \"As a site administrator, I want to control which roles can view specific migrations so that content leads only see migrations relevant to them.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"migrate_permissions.info.yml declares the submodule with dependency on migrate_suite\",\n        \"Module dynamically generates permissions in a permission callback: view migration {migration_id} for each migration plugin instance\",\n        \"Permissions appear in Drupal's standard permissions page (/admin/people/permissions) under a \\\"Migrate Suite\\\" group\",\n        \"Dashboard (US-002) filters the migration list based on the user's per-migration view permissions\",\n        \"Detail page (US-003) checks per-migration view permission before displaying\",\n        \"A user with view migrate suite dashboard permission but without any per-migration permissions sees an empty dashboard with a help message\",\n        \"A user with administer migrations (from migrate_tools) or administer site configuration bypasses per-migration checks\",\n        \"Permission names are derived from the migration plugin ID (machine-safe)\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 4,\n      \"passes\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-005\",\n      \"title\": \"Per-migration run permissions\",\n      \"description\": \"As a site administrator, I want to control which roles can execute or rollback specific migrations so that only authorized users can trigger imports.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Dynamic permissions generated: run migration {migration_id} and rollback migration {migration_id} for each migration\",\n        \"Dashboard row shows \\\"Run\\\" and \\\"Rollback\\\" action buttons only if user has the corresponding permission\",\n        \"Run action triggers a batch import of the migration and redirects to a batch progress page\",\n        \"Rollback action triggers a batch rollback and redirects to a batch progress page\",\n        \"Confirmation form shown before run/rollback with migration label and item count\",\n        \"administer migrations permission bypasses per-migration run/rollback checks\",\n        \"Actions respect migration dependencies (warn if dependent migrations haven't run)\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 5,\n      \"passes\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-006\",\n      \"title\": \"Permission matrix UI\",\n      \"description\": \"As a site administrator, I want a matrix view of migration permissions so that I can quickly see and configure which roles have access to which migrations.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Route at /admin/structure/migrate-suite/permissions with title \\\"Migration Permissions\\\"\",\n        \"Matrix table: rows = migrations (grouped by migration group), columns = roles\",\n        \"Each cell shows checkboxes for: view, run, rollback\",\n        \"Form saves permissions via Drupal's user_role_grant_permissions / user_role_revoke_permissions API\",\n        \"Matrix is filterable by migration group\",\n        \"Requires administer permissions permission to access\",\n        \"Changes are logged to watchdog\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 6,\n      \"passes\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-007\",\n      \"title\": \"Migration health indicators\",\n      \"description\": \"As a site administrator, I want to see at-a-glance health badges on each migration so that I can identify problems quickly.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"migrate_health.info.yml declares the submodule with dependency on migrate_suite\",\n        \"Each migration on the dashboard shows a health badge: healthy (green), stale (yellow), failing (red)\",\n        \"Healthy: migration has run within configured threshold AND failure rate is below configured threshold\",\n        \"Stale: migration has not run within the configured \\\"stale after X days\\\" threshold (default: 7 days)\",\n        \"Failing: migration's failure rate (failed items / total items) exceeds configured threshold (default: 5%)\",\n        \"Health thresholds configurable via settings form at /admin/structure/migrate-suite/settings\",\n        \"Settings form fields: stale threshold (days, default 7), failure rate threshold (percentage, default 5)\",\n        \"Health is computed on dashboard load from migrate_suite_run_log and map table data (no separate cron task in MVP)\",\n        \"Aggregate health summary at top of dashboard: \\\"X healthy, Y stale, Z failing\\\"\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 7,\n      \"passes\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-008\",\n      \"title\": \"Failed item tracking\",\n      \"description\": \"As a site administrator, I want to see which items failed to import with their error details so that I can take corrective action.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Migration detail page (US-003) shows a \\\"Failed Items\\\" tab\",\n        \"Tab lists items from migrate_map_{migration_id} where source_row_status = 2 (MigrateIdMapInterface::STATUS_FAILED)\",\n        \"Columns: source ID(s), error message (from migrate_message_{migration_id}), last attempt timestamp\",\n        \"Failed item count shown as a badge on the tab header\",\n        \"Filter by source ID text search\",\n        \"Pager: 50 items per page\",\n        \"\\\"Reset status\\\" bulk action to mark selected failed items for retry (sets source_row_status back to 0)\",\n        \"Reset action requires run migration {migration_id} permission (from migrate_permissions, or administer migrations if migrate_permissions is not installed)\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 8,\n      \"passes\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-009\",\n      \"title\": \"Content provenance pseudo-field on migrated entities\",\n      \"description\": \"As a content editor, I want to see migration provenance information on entity edit/view pages so that I can tell where content came from and when it was imported.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"migrate_source_field.info.yml declares the submodule with dependency on migrate_suite\",\n        \"Module implements hook_entity_extra_field_info() to register a \\\"Migration provenance\\\" pseudo-field on node entities\",\n        \"Pseudo-field is configurable per content type via \\\"Manage display\\\" (can be shown/hidden, reordered)\",\n        \"When displayed, shows a fieldset with: migration label (linked to detail page if user has permission), import date (from map table last_imported), source ID(s)\",\n        \"If entity is not found in any migrate_map_* table, pseudo-field is hidden (no empty fieldset)\",\n        \"Provenance data is computed at render time by querying map tables (not stored redundantly)\",\n        \"Results are cached per entity with appropriate cache tags (invalidated on migration run)\",\n        \"Works on both entity canonical view and edit form\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 9,\n      \"passes\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-010\",\n      \"title\": \"Original source link field\",\n      \"description\": \"As a content editor, I want a link back to the original content on the source platform so that I can compare migrated content with the original.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Configurable source URL pattern per migration via settings form, supporting a [source_id] token (e.g., https://old-site.com/node/[source_id])\",\n        \"Settings stored in migrate_suite.settings config, keyed by migration ID\",\n        \"Source link displayed within the provenance pseudo-field (US-009) as a clickable URL\",\n        \"Link opens in a new tab (target=\\\"_blank\\\" with rel=\\\"noopener\\\")\",\n        \"If no URL pattern is configured for a migration, the source link row is omitted (not shown as empty)\",\n        \"URL pattern configuration form accessible at /admin/structure/migrate-suite/settings/source-links\",\n        \"Form lists all migrations with a text field for each URL pattern\",\n        \"Token replacement handles multiple source IDs (composite keys) by joining with /\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 10,\n      \"passes\": false\n    }\n  ]\n}","numLines":176,"startLine":1,"totalLines":176}}}
