{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014BWwGfyWziK7nc3W98vjox","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→<?php\n     2→\n     3→declare(strict_types=1);\n     4→\n     5→namespace Drupal\\migrate_suite\\EventSubscriber;\n     6→\n     7→use Drupal\\Component\\Datetime\\TimeInterface;\n     8→use Drupal\\Core\\Database\\Connection;\n     9→use Drupal\\migrate\\Event\\MigrateEvents;\n    10→use Drupal\\migrate\\Event\\MigrateImportEvent;\n    11→use Drupal\\migrate\\Event\\MigratePostRowSaveEvent;\n    12→use Drupal\\migrate\\Event\\MigratePreRowSaveEvent;\n    13→use Drupal\\migrate\\Plugin\\MigrateIdMapInterface;\n    14→use Symfony\\Component\\EventDispatcher\\EventSubscriberInterface;\n    15→\n    16→/**\n    17→ * Logs migration run data to migrate_suite_run_log.\n    18→ */\n    19→class MigrateRunLogger implements EventSubscriberInterface {\n    20→\n    21→  /**\n    22→   * Tracks the current run log IDs keyed by migration ID.\n    23→   *\n    24→   * @var array<string, int>\n    25→   */\n    26→  protected array $activeRuns = [];\n    27→\n    28→  /**\n    29→   * Tracks row-level counters keyed by migration ID.\n    30→   *\n    31→   * @var array<string, array{processed: int, created: int, updated: int, failed: int}>\n    32→   */\n    33→  protected array $counters = [];\n    34→\n    35→  /**\n    36→   * Constructs a MigrateRunLogger object.\n    37→   *\n    38→   * @param \\Drupal\\Core\\Database\\Connection $database\n    39→   *   The database connection.\n    40→   * @param \\Drupal\\Component\\Datetime\\TimeInterface $time\n    41→   *   The time service.\n    42→   */\n    43→  public function __construct(\n    44→    protected readonly Connection $database,\n    45→    protected readonly TimeInterface $time,\n    46→  ) {}\n    47→\n    48→  /**\n    49→   * {@inheritdoc}\n    50→   */\n    51→  public static function getSubscribedEvents(): array {\n    52→    return [\n    53→      MigrateEvents::PRE_IMPORT => ['onPreImport'],\n    54→      MigrateEvents::POST_IMPORT => ['onPostImport'],\n    55→      MigrateEvents::PRE_ROW_SAVE => ['onPreRowSave'],\n    56→      MigrateEvents::POST_ROW_SAVE => ['onPostRowSave'],\n    57→    ];\n    58→  }\n    59→\n    60→  /**\n    61→   * Reacts to the pre-import event.\n    62→   *\n    63→   * @param \\Drupal\\migrate\\Event\\MigrateImportEvent $event\n    64→   *   The import event.\n    65→   */\n    66→  public function onPreImport(MigrateImportEvent $event): void {\n    67→    $migrationId = $event->getMigration()->id();\n    68→\n    69→    $this->counters[$migrationId] = [\n    70→      'processed' => 0,\n    71→      'created' => 0,\n    72→      'updated' => 0,\n    73→      'failed' => 0,\n    74→    ];\n    75→\n    76→    $id = $this->database->insert('migrate_suite_run_log')\n    77→      ->fields([\n    78→        'migration_id' => $migrationId,\n    79→        'status' => 'running',\n    80→        'started' => $this->time->getRequestTime(),\n    81→      ])\n    82→      ->execute();\n    83→\n    84→    $this->activeRuns[$migrationId] = (int) $id;\n    85→  }\n    86→\n    87→  /**\n    88→   * Reacts to the post-import event.\n    89→   *\n    90→   * @param \\Drupal\\migrate\\Event\\MigrateImportEvent $event\n    91→   *   The import event.\n    92→   */\n    93→  public function onPostImport(MigrateImportEvent $event): void {\n    94→    $migrationId = $event->getMigration()->id();\n    95→\n    96→    if (!isset($this->activeRuns[$migrationId])) {\n    97→      return;\n    98→    }\n    99→\n   100→    $counters = $this->counters[$migrationId] ?? [\n   101→      'processed' => 0,\n   102→      'created' => 0,\n   103→      'updated' => 0,\n   104→      'failed' => 0,\n   105→    ];\n   106→\n   107→    $status = $counters['failed'] > 0 ? 'failed' : 'completed';\n   108→\n   109→    $this->database->update('migrate_suite_run_log')\n   110→      ->fields([\n   111→        'status' => $status,\n   112→        'finished' => $this->time->getRequestTime(),\n   113→        'items_processed' => $counters['processed'],\n   114→        'items_created' => $counters['created'],\n   115→        'items_updated' => $counters['updated'],\n   116→        'items_failed' => $counters['failed'],\n   117→      ])\n   118→      ->condition('id', $this->activeRuns[$migrationId])\n   119→      ->execute();\n   120→\n   121→    unset($this->activeRuns[$migrationId], $this->counters[$migrationId]);\n   122→  }\n   123→\n   124→  /**\n   125→   * Reacts to the pre-row-save event.\n   126→   *\n   127→   * @param \\Drupal\\migrate\\Event\\MigratePreRowSaveEvent $event\n   128→   *   The pre-row-save event.\n   129→   */\n   130→  public function onPreRowSave(MigratePreRowSaveEvent $event): void {\n   131→    // Track that a row is being processed.\n   132→    $migrationId = $event->getMigration()->id();\n   133→    if (isset($this->counters[$migrationId])) {\n   134→      $this->counters[$migrationId]['processed']++;\n   135→    }\n   136→  }\n   137→\n   138→  /**\n   139→   * Reacts to the post-row-save event.\n   140→   *\n   141→   * @param \\Drupal\\migrate\\Event\\MigratePostRowSaveEvent $event\n   142→   *   The post-row-save event.\n   143→   */\n   144→  public function onPostRowSave(MigratePostRowSaveEvent $event): void {\n   145→    $migrationId = $event->getMigration()->id();\n   146→\n   147→    if (!isset($this->counters[$migrationId])) {\n   148→      return;\n   149→    }\n   150→\n   151→    $idMap = $event->getRow()->getIdMap();\n   152→    $status = $idMap['source_row_status'] ?? MigrateIdMapInterface::STATUS_IMPORTED;\n   153→\n   154→    switch ($status) {\n   155→      case MigrateIdMapInterface::STATUS_IMPORTED:\n   156→        // Determine if this is a create or update based on destination IDs.\n   157→        $destIds = $event->getDestinationIdValues();\n   158→        if (!empty($destIds)) {\n   159→          // Check if the row had pre-existing destination IDs (update).\n   160→          $previousDestIds = $event->getRow()->getDestination();\n   161→          if (!empty($previousDestIds)) {\n   162→            $this->counters[$migrationId]['updated']++;\n   163→          }\n   164→          else {\n   165→            $this->counters[$migrationId]['created']++;\n   166→          }\n   167→        }\n   168→        break;\n   169→\n   170→      case MigrateIdMapInterface::STATUS_FAILED:\n   171→        $this->counters[$migrationId]['failed']++;\n   172→        break;\n   173→    }\n   174→  }\n   175→\n   176→}\n   177→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01K4BTcZkXfLmZoZb78Si7ST","session_id":"947754a4-35aa-442f-a4b8-f81a7a0a67f9","uuid":"cb01059f-9f75-47bc-a62c-fddde391b2d5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K4BTcZkXfLmZoZb78Si7ST","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me create a detailed summary for you:\n\n## Codebase Structure Exploration - Complete Summary\n\n### 1. Directory Layout\n\nThe codebase is organized as follows:\n\n```\n/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/\n├── migrate_suite.info.yml          (Main module metadata)\n├── migrate_suite.module             (Main module hooks - empty)\n├── migrate_suite.install            (Schema definitions)\n├── migrate_suite.services.yml       (Service definitions)\n│\n├── src/\n│   ├── Service/\n│   │   ├── MigrateMapQuery.php      (Map table queries)\n│   │   └── MigrateMessageQuery.php  (Message table queries)\n│   └── EventSubscriber/\n│       └── MigrateRunLogger.php     (Event listener for migration runs)\n│\n└── modules/\n    ├── migrate_admin/\n    │   ├── migrate_admin.info.yml\n    │   ├── migrate_admin.module\n    │   ├── migrate_admin.services.yml\n    │   ├── migrate_admin.routing.yml\n    │   ├── migrate_admin.permissions.yml\n    │   ├── migrate_admin.libraries.yml\n    │   ├── css/migrate_admin.css\n    │   └── src/\n    │       ├── Controller/\n    │       │   ├── MigrationDashboardController.php\n    │       │   └── MigrationDetailController.php\n    │       └── Form/\n    │           ├── MigrationRunConfirmForm.php\n    │           ├── MigrationRollbackConfirmForm.php\n    │           └── FailedItemsResetForm.php\n    │\n    ├── migrate_health/\n    │   ├── migrate_health.info.yml\n    │   ├── migrate_health.module\n    │   ├── migrate_health.services.yml\n    │   ├── migrate_health.routing.yml\n    │   ├── migrate_health.links.menu.yml\n    │   ├── migrate_health.libraries.yml\n    │   ├── css/migrate_health.css\n    │   └── src/\n    │       ├── Form/\n    │       │   └── HealthSettingsForm.php\n    │       └── Service/\n    │           └── MigrationHealthAnalyzer.php\n    │\n    └── migrate_permissions/\n        ├── migrate_permissions.info.yml\n        ├── migrate_permissions.module\n        ├── migrate_permissions.services.yml\n        ├── migrate_permissions.routing.yml\n        ├── migrate_permissions.permissions.yml\n        ├── migrate_permissions.links.menu.yml\n        ├── migrate_permissions.libraries.yml\n        ├── css/migrate_permissions.css\n        └── src/\n            ├── Form/\n            │   └── PermissionMatrixForm.php\n            ├── MigrateAccessCheck.php\n            └── MigratePermissions.php\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Main Services Configuration\n\n**File: `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/migrate_suite.services.yml`**\n\n```yaml\nservices:\n  migrate_suite.map_query:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_suite\\Service\\MigrateMapQuery\n    arguments: ['@database', '@plugin.manager.migration']\n\n  migrate_suite.message_query:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_suite\\Service\\MigrateMessageQuery\n    arguments: ['@database']\n\n  migrate_suite.run_logger:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_suite\\EventSubscriber\\MigrateRunLogger\n    arguments: ['@database', '@datetime.time']\n    tags:\n      - { name: event_subscriber }\n```\n\nThis defines three core services:\n1. **map_query**: Handles migration map table queries\n2. **message_query**: Handles migration message table queries\n3. **run_logger**: Event subscriber that logs migration run statistics\n\n---\n\n### 3. MigrateMapQuery Service\n\n**File: `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/src/Service/MigrateMapQuery.php`**\n\nPublic methods provided by this service:\n\n```php\npublic function lookupDestinationIds(string $migrationId, array $sourceIdValues): array\n// Looks up destination IDs by source ID in the map table\n\npublic function listImportedItems(string $migrationId, int $limit = 50, int $offset = 0): array\n// Lists all imported items for a migration with pagination\n\npublic function countItemsByStatus(string $migrationId): array\n// Counts items by status (imported, needs_update, failed)\n// Returns array with keys: 'imported', 'needs_update', 'failed'\n```\n\nProtected helper method:\n```php\nprotected function getMapTableName(string $migrationId): string\n// Returns the map table name (e.g., 'migrate_map_migration_id')\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Submodule Structure Example: migrate_health\n\n**File: `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_health/migrate_health.info.yml`**\n\n```yaml\nname: Migrate Health\ntype: module\ndescription: 'Health badges, stale detection, and failed item tracking for migrations.'\npackage: Migrate Suite\ncore_version_requirement: ^10.4 || ^11\ndependencies:\n  - migrate_suite:migrate_suite\n```\n\n**File: `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_health/migrate_health.module`**\n\n```php\n<?php\n/**\n * @file\n * Provides health monitoring and badges for migrations.\n */\ndeclare(strict_types=1);\n```\n(Minimal module file with just documentation)\n\n**File: `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_health/migrate_health.services.yml`**\n\n```yaml\nservices:\n  migrate_health.analyzer:\n    class: Drupal\\migrate_health\\Service\\MigrationHealthAnalyzer\n    arguments: ['@database', '@config.factory', '@datetime.time']\n```\n\n**File: `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_health/migrate_health.routing.yml`**\n\n```yaml\nmigrate_health.settings:\n  path: '/admin/structure/migrate-suite/settings'\n  defaults:\n    _form: '\\Drupal\\migrate_health\\Form\\HealthSettingsForm'\n    _title: 'Migration Health Settings'\n  requirements:\n    _permission: 'administer site configuration'\n```\n\n**File: `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_health/migrate_health.links.menu.yml`**\n\n```yaml\nmigrate_health.settings:\n  title: 'Migration Health Settings'\n  description: 'Configure health thresholds for migration monitoring.'\n  route_name: migrate_health.settings\n  parent: system.admin_structure\n  weight: 52\n```\n\n**File: `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_health/src/Service/MigrationHealthAnalyzer.php`**\n\nThis service provides health analysis with these public methods:\n\n```php\npublic function getHealth(string $migrationId): string\n// Returns: 'healthy', 'stale', or 'failing'\n\npublic function getHealthForMultiple(array $migrationIds): array\n// Returns associative array: migrationId => status\n\npublic function getAggregateSummary(array $healthStatuses): array\n// Returns: ['healthy' => count, 'stale' => count, 'failing' => count]\n\nprotected function isFailingMigration(string $migrationId, float $threshold): bool\n// Checks if failure rate exceeds threshold (percentage)\n\nprotected function isStaleMigration(string $migrationId, int $thresholdDays): bool\n// Checks if migration hasn't run within threshold days\n```\n\nHealth status constants:\n- `HEALTHY = 'healthy'`\n- `STALE = 'stale'`\n- `FAILING = 'failing'`\n\n---\n\n### 5. MigrationDetailController\n\n**File: `/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/migrate_admin/src/Controller/MigrationDetailController.php`**\n\nThis controller handles the detail pages for individual migrations. Key public methods:\n\n```php\npublic function detail(string $migration_id, Request $request): array\n// Main detail page showing summary, status, and imported items\n\npublic function messages(string $migration_id, Request $request): array\n// Messages page showing migration messages/logs\n\npublic function failedItems(string $migration_id, Request $request): array\n// Failed items page with search/filtering\n```\n\nKey protected methods:\n- `buildTabs()`: Creates tab navigation (Items/Messages/Failed)\n- `buildImportedItemsSection()`: Builds the imported items table with filters and pager\n- `buildMessagesSection()`: Builds messages table with severity filtering\n- `buildFailedItemsSection()`: Builds failed items table with search\n- `loadMigration()`: Loads migration and checks access permissions\n- `getMigrationStatus()`: Gets current migration status (idle, importing, rolling_back, completed, failed)\n- `getLastRunStats()`: Fetches last run statistics from run_log table\n- `buildStatusBadge()`: Creates colored status badges\n- `buildEntityLink()`: Attempts to create links to destination entities\n- `getRowStatusLabel()`: Maps status codes to human-readable labels\n- `getSeverityIcon()`: Creates severity badges for messages\n- `buildPager()`: Creates pagination controls\n- `buildItemFilterForm()`: Creates filters for imported items (search + status)\n- `buildMessageFilterForm()`: Creates filters for messages (severity)\n- `buildFailedItemFilterForm()`: Creates search filter for failed items\n\nThe controller integrates with:\n- `MigrateAccessCheck` (from migrate_permissions module if installed)\n- The migration plugin manager\n- The database connection\n- The date formatter service\n\nConfiguration constants:\n- `ITEMS_PER_PAGE = 50`\n\n---\n\n### 6. Supporting Services\n\n**MigrateMessageQuery** (`/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/src/Service/MigrateMessageQuery.php`)\n\n```php\npublic function getMessages(string $migrationId, int $limit = 50, int $offset = 0): array\n// Fetches messages for a migration\n\npublic function getMessagesForSourceId(string $migrationId, array $sourceIdValues): array\n// Fetches messages for a specific source ID\n```\n\n**MigrateRunLogger** (`/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/src/EventSubscriber/MigrateRunLogger.php`)\n\nSubscribes to these migration events:\n- `MigrateEvents::PRE_IMPORT` → `onPreImport()`\n- `MigrateEvents::POST_IMPORT` → `onPostImport()`\n- `MigrateEvents::PRE_ROW_SAVE` → `onPreRowSave()`\n- `MigrateEvents::POST_ROW_SAVE` → `onPostRowSave()`\n\nLogs to the `migrate_suite_run_log` table with fields:\n- `id` (primary key)\n- `migration_id`\n- `status` (idle, running, completed, failed)\n- `started` (timestamp)\n- `finished` (timestamp)\n- `items_processed`\n- `items_created`\n- `items_updated`\n- `items_failed`\n\n---\n\n### 7. Root Module Files\n\n**migrate_suite.info.yml:**\n```yaml\nname: Migrate Suite\ntype: module\ndescription: 'Administration dashboard for managing and monitoring Drupal migrations.'\npackage: Migration\ncore_version_requirement: ^10.4 || ^11\ndependencies:\n  - drupal:migrate\n```\n\n**migrate_suite.install:**\nDefines the `migrate_suite_run_log` schema with migration run history tracking.\n\nThis establishes the Migrate Suite as the core module with three submodules providing additional functionality: admin dashboards, health monitoring, and access control."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ab8a30d204697aba3 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 53027\ntool_uses: 26\nduration_ms: 51588</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"947754a4-35aa-442f-a4b8-f81a7a0a67f9","uuid":"f48ced2d-9060-4114-8311-7ceed4289092","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the codebase structure for me. I need to understand:\n1. The directory layout under /Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/modules/\n2. The contents of migrate_suite.services.yml\n3. The MigrateMapQuery service (src/Service/MigrateMapQuery.php) - specifically what methods it provides\n4. How other submodules are structured (pick migrate_health as an example - info.yml, module file, services.yml)\n5. The MigrationDetailController.php to understand how the detail page works\n\nReturn all file contents you find.","agentId":"ab8a30d204697aba3","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me create a detailed summary for you:\n\n## Codebase Structure Exploration - Complete Summary\n\n### 1. Directory Layout\n\nThe codebase is organized as follows:\n\n```\n/Users/pieter/Projects/drupal-migrate_suite/\n├── migrate_suite.info.yml          (Main module metadata)\n├── migrate_suite.module             (Main module hooks - empty)\n├── 