{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Hs4cFMGacXH5Fuk1ry3P9c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good understanding of the codebase. Let me implement US-009: Content provenance pseudo-field on migrated entities.\n\nI need to:\n1. Create `modules/migrate_source_field/migrate_source_field.info.yml`\n2. Create `modules/migrate_source_field/migrate_source_field.module` - with hook_entity_extra_field_info() and hook_entity_view() / hook_form_alter()\n3. Create a service that queries map tables to find provenance data for an entity\n\nLet me think about the approach:\n\n- `hook_entity_extra_field_info()` - registers a \"Migration provenance\" pseudo-field on node entities\n\n\n- The pseudo-field should be configurable per content type through the display settings, and when rendered it displays the migration label as a link, the import date, and source IDs\n- I'll query all migrate_map_* tables at render time to find the entity and retrieve the migration ID and source IDs, then implement caching with custom cache tags that get invalidated when migrations run\n- The field should work on both the canonical view and edit form, and remain hidden if the entity isn't found in any map table\n\nFor the cache strategy, I'm thinking a general `migrate_suite:provenance` tag that invalidates whenever any migration completes would be simpler than trying to track which specific migration owns each entity, since we don't know that until after querying the tables anyway.\n\nNow I'm setting up the module structure and implementation files...\n\nFor the extra field registration, I'll use `hook_entity_extra_field_info()` to declare it for all node bundles, then handle both the view and form display through `hook_entity_view()` and `hook_form_alter()` respectively.\n\nNow I'm realizing I need to reverse-lookup migrations — given a destination entity, find which migration created it. The existing MigrateMapQuery service only goes source to destination, so I'll create a ProvenanceLookup service that iterates through all migration plugins, filters by destination entity type, and queries each migration map table to find the source.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3284,"cache_read_input_tokens":38964,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3284},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"947754a4-35aa-442f-a4b8-f81a7a0a67f9","uuid":"3802d606-7082-46bb-8f03-494b4178aaff"}
